B.uo=new A.bp(B.eP,["trevouxapp","Accueil","Scanner QR","Nos lieux","Je continue","C'est parti !","D\xe9marrer le guidage","Je continue","\xcates-vous pr\xeat ?","L'aventure commence dans...","Parcours culturel","Chasse en for\xeat","Troph\xe9es","Ma progression","Vos lieux visit\xe9s et vos troph\xe9es de parcours","Lieux visit\xe9s"," lieux visit\xe9s sur ","Parcours & troph\xe9es","Verrouill\xe9","D\xe9bloqu\xe9 !","Tenter ma chance","Voir mon lot","Bient\xf4t disponible","Tournez la roue !","Lancer la roue","Bravo !","Votre code","Pr\xe9sentez ce code \xe0 un commer\xe7ant partenaire pour profiter de votre lot.","Lot d\xe9j\xe0 obtenu","-10% dans un restaurant partenaire","Une boisson offerte","Un dessert offert","-5% dans un commerce partenaire","Un souvenir surprise","Retentez votre chance une prochaine fois","D'accord","Un seul tirage par appareil et par jour. R\xe9essaie demain !","La roue de r\xe9compense n'est pas disponible pour le moment.","Impossible de tourner la roue pour le moment. V\xe9rifie ta connexion et r\xe9essaie.","Le saviez-vous ?","D\xe9couvrez le ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Balade au bord de la Sa\xf4ne","Le march\xe9 du samedi matin","Chers voyageurs, bienvenue \xe0 Tr\xe9voux ! Vous allez d\xe9couvrir les secrets et l'histoire de cette merveilleuse ville m\xe9di\xe9vale.","C'est parti !","Avant de d\xe9buter votre p\xe9riple, veuillez s\xe9lectionner votre parcours.","Parcours culturel","Parcours ludique","Une derni\xe8re chose.. Quel est votre moyen de locomotion ?","Je suis \xe0 v\xe9lo","Je suis en voiture","Je suis pi\xe9ton","\ud83c\udff0 Qu\xeate des Gardiens\nde la For\xeat de Tr\xe9voux","\u23f1\ufe0f Temps restant: 15:00","\ud83d\udcc8 Votre progression","0/5","\ud83c\udfc5 Collections de badges","\ud83d\ude80 Commencer l'Aventure","\ud83d\udcf1 Scanner le QR Code","\ud83d\udd04 Nouvelle tentative","Titre de l'\xe9tape","Description de l'\xe9tape","\ud83c\udfa7 \xc9couter l'histoire","\ud83d\udca1 aide","\ud83d\udca1 Indice appara\xeet ici","D\xe9couvrez l'histoire de Tr\xe9voux \xe0 travers cette aventure interactive ! \ud83c\udf1f","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Panorama de l'Orme","La rue des Arts","L'ancien parlement des Dombes","Le Lavoir de Tr\xe9voux","La Tour de l'horloge","L'Eglise","La Porte de Villars","Aller visiter","Aper\xe7u en images","Le Ch\xe2teau",u.u,"\ud83e\udded Commencer la navigation","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Scannez et D\xe9couvrez","\ud83c\udfc6 F\xe9licitations, Chevalier !","Message de f\xe9licitations","\ud83d\udcca Vos Statistiques","Statistiques de la qu\xeate","\ud83d\udcdc Votre Certificat","\ud83d\udcbe T\xe9l\xe9charger le Certificat","\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Badges Obtenus","\ud83d\udcf1 Partager mes R\xe9sultats","\ud83d\udd04 Recommencer la Qu\xeate","Continuer la visite","Merci d'avoir particip\xe9 \xe0 cette aventure dans la for\xeat de Tr\xe9voux !","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : 10 minutes","Dur\xe9e totale restante : 30 minutes","Continuer","Le Ch\xe2teau","Chers Voyageurs, vous \xeates sur le point de p\xe9n\xe9trer au c\u0153ur de l\u2019histoire de Tr\xe9voux en d\xe9couvrant son ch\xe2teau m\xe9di\xe9val. Dominant la ville et la Sa\xf4ne, cet \xe9difice embl\xe9matique t\xe9moigne du pass\xe9 prestigieux de l\u2019ancienne capitale de la Principaut\xe9 de Dombes.","Avant d\u2019atteindre ses remparts, laissez-vous charmer par une agr\xe9able promenade \xe0 travers les ruelles pittoresques de la vieille ville. Une fois sur place, profitez d\u2019un panorama exceptionnel et plongez dans les r\xe9cits fascinants de ce lieu charg\xe9 d\u2019histoire. Pr\xe9parez-vous \xe0 un voyage dans le temps o\xf9 chaque pierre raconte une histoire !","D\xe9marrer la navigation","Naviguation2","Open navigation drawer","Close navigation drawer","Android Studio","android.studio@android.com","Navigation header","Settings","Home","Gallery","Slideshow","MapsActivity","Vous \xeates d\xe9sormais devant le ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux, symbole de puissance et t\xe9moin de cinq si\xe8cles d'histoire extraordinaire ! Ce ch\xe2teau fort fut \xe9difi\xe9 vers 1300 par les Sires de Thoire-Villars pour surveiller le port et le p\xe9age sur la Sa\xf4ne. Mais c'est en 1402 que tout bascule : le dernier des Thoire-Villars vend le fief \xe0 Louis II de Bourbon, donnant naissance \xe0 l'une des plus fascinantes principaut\xe9s d'Europe.","Construit en deux campagnes principales au XIVe si\xe8cle, ce ch\xe2teau fort de pierre est un \xe9difice imposant class\xe9 Monument historique d\xe8s 1913. Son donjon octogonal unique, d\xe9cor\xe9 de pierres dor\xe9es et blanches, culminait autrefois \xe0 28 m\xe8tres - aujourd'hui amput\xe9 \xe0 16 m\xe8tres suite \xe0 la R\xe9volution - et offre toujours un panorama exceptionnel sur la vall\xe9e de la Sa\xf4ne, le plateau de Dombes et le Beaujolais. L'ensemble t\xe9moigne de sa triple fonction : b\xe2timent militaire fortifi\xe9, r\xe9sidence seigneuriale et symbole de pouvoir souverain.","Car Tr\xe9voux ne fut pas une simple ville : elle devint capitale de la Principaut\xe9 de Dombes, un ancien \xc9tat souverain \xe0 la fronti\xe8re entre le royaume de France et le Saint-Empire romain germanique ! Malgr\xe9 une annexion au royaume de France entre 1523 et 1560, la Principaut\xe9 de Dombes acquiert son ind\xe9pendance politique et conserve ses privil\xe8ges jusqu'en 1762, date de son rattachement d\xe9finitif \xe0 la France par Louis-Charles de Bourbon qui \xe9change la souverainet\xe9 avec Louis XV.",'Imaginez : depuis ce ch\xe2teau, les princes souverains de Dombes battaient monnaie, rendaient justice, levaient des imp\xf4ts et entretenaient leur propre diplomatie ! Un rempart en brique et en pierre entoure alors la ville et quatre portes y sont am\xe9nag\xe9es transformant Tr\xe9voux en v\xe9ritable cit\xe9-\xc9tat fortifi\xe9e. Le ch\xe2teau fut le c\u0153ur de cette cit\xe9 qui fit de Tr\xe9voux le "Monaco de l\'\xe9poque" gr\xe2ce \xe0 son commerce et sa fiscalit\xe9 avantageuse.',"La Grande Mademoiselle (Anne Marie Louise d'Orl\xe9ans), cousine de Louis XIV, fit de Tr\xe9voux l'\xe9picentre d'un scandale royal ! En 1669, elle avait donn\xe9 sous forme d'apanage la principaut\xe9 des Dombes au duc de Lauzun qu'elle comptait \xe9pouser. Mais leur amour contraria le Roi-Soleil qui fit emprisonner Lauzun \xe0 Pignerol ! En 1681, sous la pression du roi, il dut renoncer aux apanages re\xe7us pour \xeatre lib\xe9r\xe9. Cette histoire d'amour impossible entre la richissime h\xe9riti\xe8re et le courtisan ambitieux alimenta les chroniques de Versailles et fit de Tr\xe9voux le th\xe9\xe2tre d'une des plus belles histoires d'amour contrari\xe9es de l'Ancien R\xe9gime !","La Principaut\xe9 de Dombes \xe9tait un v\xe9ritable \xc9tat souverain qui a exist\xe9 pendant plus de trois si\xe8cles, des Bourbons en 1402 jusqu'au rattachement \xe0 la France en 1762 ! Elle avait ses propres lois, sa monnaie, son parlement et m\xeame sa diplomatie. Les princes de Dombes \xe9taient si puissants qu'ils pouvaient d\xe9clarer la guerre, signer des trait\xe9s et recevoir des ambassadeurs \xe9trangers. Cette souverainet\xe9 quasi-totale \xe9tait unique en France et faisait de Tr\xe9voux une capitale \xe0 part enti\xe8re, rivalisant - \xe0 son \xe9chelle - avec certaines cours princi\xe8res d'Allemagne ou d'Italie !","Le donjon octogonal du ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux est une prouesse architecturale rare ! Cette forme g\xe9om\xe9trique particuli\xe8re \xe9tait \xe0 la fois esth\xe9tique et strat\xe9gique : contrairement aux tours rondes classiques, l'octogone offrait plus d'angles de tir tout en r\xe9sistant mieux aux bombardements. De plus, sa construction en pierres dor\xe9es et blanches altern\xe9es (technique appel\xe9e \"appareil polychrome\") t\xe9moigne du raffinement et de la richesse de ses constructeurs. Peu de ch\xe2teaux fran\xe7ais poss\xe8dent un donjon de cette forme si sophistiqu\xe9e, ce qui fait du ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux un joyau architectural unique !","Vous \xeates au panorama de l\u2019Orme offrant une vue magnifique \xe0 flanc de colline et en surplomb de la ville. Le regard se porte naturellement sur la Sa\xf4ne (rep\xe8re A) : 9\xe8me plus longue rivi\xe8re de France avec ses presque 500 km. Elle doit son nom \xe0 la d\xe9esse celte Souconna (ou Sauc-Onna) que v\xe9n\xe9raient les S\xe9quanes. Cette tribu celte contr\xf4lait jadis une grande partie des territoires travers\xe9s par ce cours d\u2019eau. Les romains, prenant possession des lieux et pla\xe7ant cette tribu sous leur autorit\xe9, ont alors d\xe9cid\xe9 de nommer la rivi\xe8re ainsi.","Aux abords de la Sa\xf4ne, on distingue le chemin de halage (rep\xe8re B) qui permettait autrefois d\u2019encadrer le transport de marchandises par p\xe9niches. Le d\xe9bit relativement calme de la Sa\xf4ne facilitait ce mode de circulation. Aujourd\u2019hui, les p\xe9niches ont fait place aux bateaux de croisi\xe8re que l\u2019on peut apercevoir r\xe9guli\xe8rement amarr\xe9s \xe0 la halte fluviale (rep\xe8re C) et \xe0 2 pas du camping (rep\xe8re D).","Parmi les toitures de la ville, on distingue d\u2019embl\xe9e le d\xf4me de l\u2019h\xf4pital Montpensier (rep\xe8re D) fond\xe9 il y a de cela 350 ans par la duchesse de Montpensier, s\u0153ur de Louis XIII et cousine du roi Louis XIV, lorsqu\u2019elle r\xe9gnait en souveraine sur toute la Dombes. L\u2019h\xf4pital fut \xe9difi\xe9 sur la muraille m\xe9di\xe9vale de la ville et int\xe9gra ainsi cette grosse tour ronde de fortification.","Enjambant la Sa\xf4ne, une passerelle (rep\xe8re E) permet aux pi\xe9tons et aux cyclistes de se rendre \xe0 Quincieux et, au passage, de changer de d\xe9partement : bienvenue dans le Rh\xf4ne ! Au milieu de la passerelle, vous serez au Point Kilom\xe9trique 31 (PK 31) de la Sa\xf4ne. Autrement dit, en regardant vers la gauche, il reste 31 km avant la confluence de la rivi\xe8re dans le Rh\xf4ne, \xe0 Lyon. Ce sera la fin de son voyage commenc\xe9 452km en amont depuis sa source, dans les Vosges, \xe0 486m d\u2019altitude.","-L\u2019arbre de la justice. L\u2019Orme est un arbre d\u2019ornement noble dont le bois est pr\xe9cieux et d\u2019une grande duret\xe9. Longtemps utilis\xe9 en marine pour les coques de bateau, il sert \xe9galement pour la fabrication de meubles raffin\xe9s. Anecdote int\xe9ressante \xe0 se souvenir : au Moyen-Age, l\u2019Orme \xe9tait appel\xe9 \xab l\u2019arbre de la justice \xbb parce que c\u2019est sous cet arbre que les juges des seigneurs rendaient la justice. Il \xe9tait donc tr\xe8s fr\xe9quent d\u2019en trouver \xe0 proximit\xe9 des ch\xe2teaux.","-Fleuve ou rivi\xe8re ? Malgr\xe9 sa largeur (entre 100 et 200m) et sa profondeur (jusqu\u2019\xe0 8m), la Sa\xf4ne est une rivi\xe8re et non pas un fleuve comme on pourrait le croire ou l\u2019entendre de-ci de-l\xe0. En effet, un fleuve est \xab un cours d'eau finissant dans la mer ou l\u2019oc\xe9an \xbb. La Sa\xf4ne fait ainsi partie des nombreuses rivi\xe8res alimentant le Rh\xf4ne qui, lui, est un fleuve se jetant en mer m\xe9diterran\xe9e. La Sa\xf4ne se jette dans le Rh\xf4ne \xe0 Lyon ; on appelle cette jonction la confluence. Cela a d\u2019ailleurs donn\xe9 le nom de ce \xab quartier \xbb de Lyon.","-La myst\xe9rieuse boule. Avez-vous remarqu\xe9 l\u2019\xe9trange boule noire au sommet de la plus haute montagne observable de ce panorama ? Ce n\u2019est pas l\u2019\xe9toile myst\xe9rieuse de Tintin, mais un radar militaire. Il est install\xe9 au sommet du Mont Verdun (626m d\u2019altitude) ; point culminant des Monts d\u2019Or lyonnais. Il est sous contr\xf4le de la base de l\u2019arm\xe9e de l\u2019air fran\xe7aise install\xe9e sur ce secteur : la base a\xe9rienne 942 Lyon-Mont Verdun, centre de validation de commandement de l\u2019OTAN !","Vous \xeates ici au pied de la tour de l'horloge, t\xe9moin du temps qui passe et de l'organisation municipale d'autrefois ! Mais avant d'\xeatre un beffroi, cet emplacement abritait l'ancien arsenal de Tr\xe9voux. Cette tour fut en effet construite vers 1405 contre les b\xe2timents de l'arsenal pour lequel elle devait servir d'avant-corps, comme en t\xe9moignent encore les arch\xe8res cruciformes visibles sur la partie basse de l'\xe9difice, et jouait un r\xf4le important dans la d\xe9fense de la ville.","C'est en 1732 que le conseil de la ville vote un emprunt pour l'achat d'une nouvelle horloge et la refonte de la cloche \u2014 l'occasion de transf\xe9rer d\xe9finitivement le beffroi municipal dans cette tour de pierre. Son r\xf4le devint alors essentiel : les cloches sonnaient les heures, annon\xe7aient les \xe9v\xe9nements importants, appelaient la population aux assembl\xe9es. Dans une principaut\xe9 souveraine comme celle de Dombes, avoir son propre beffroi n'\xe9tait pas rien : c'\xe9tait une d\xe9claration d'autonomie en pierre et en bronze.","Les beffrois, c'\xe9tait bien plus que des tours \xe0 horloge ! Au Moyen \xc2ge et \xe0 la Renaissance, en avoir un signifiait que la ville avait arrach\xe9 ses droits \xe0 son seigneur. Ces tours convoquaient les assembl\xe9es, annon\xe7aient les f\xeates et les march\xe9s, sonnaient l'alarme en cas de danger. Dans les villes libres comme Tr\xe9voux, le beffroi \xe9tait l'\xe9quivalent la\xefc du clocher : un symbole de pouvoir \u2014 et d'ind\xe9pendance \u2014 que certains suzerains n'h\xe9sitaient pas \xe0 faire d\xe9truire en guise de punition.","Le rapport au temps au Moyen \xc2ge n'avait rien \xe0 voir avec le n\xf4tre ! Avant les horloges m\xe9caniques \u2014 qui apparaissent \xe0 la fin du XIIIe si\xe8cle \u2014 on se r\xe9glait sur les cloches des \xe9glises, qui sonnaient les offices : matines, laudes, v\xeapres... L'horloge municipale fut une vraie r\xe9volution : elle permettait de mesurer un temps \"civil\", distinct du temps religieux. Pour les marchands, artisans et banquiers qui avaient besoin de pr\xe9cision pour leurs affaires, c'\xe9tait un outil indispensable. Poss\xe9der une horloge publique, c'\xe9tait entrer dans la modernit\xe9.","Les cloches communales avaient leur propre langage. Chaque ville d\xe9veloppait ses codes : tant de coups pour un incendie, tant pour convoquer le conseil, tant pour l'ouverture du march\xe9... Les habitants reconnaissaient imm\xe9diatement le message \u2014 pas besoin de smartphone ! Ces \"conversations\" sonores cr\xe9aient une v\xe9ritable identit\xe9 municipale et renfor\xe7aient le sentiment d'appartenance \xe0 la communaut\xe9. Un art de communiquer que nos anc\xeatres ma\xeetrisaient sans r\xe9seau.","Vous \xeates l\xe0 o\xf9 se trouvait la fontaine de la ville autrefois. C\u2019est donc ici que le conseil de la ville d\xe9cida en 1730 de construire un lavoir public dont le nom \xe9voluera peu \xe0 peu : lavoir de la Font (sous-entendu de la Fontaine) puis lavoir de Lafond. Le robinet au mur permet de voir l\xe0 o\xf9 l\u2019eau naturelle arrivait autrefois et si vous \xeates curieux vous pouvez m\xeame observer la source d\u2019eau d\u2019origine.","La construction que vous voyez n\u2019est pas celle des origines : au d\xe9part le lavoir \xe9tait dispos\xe9 dans l\u2019autre sens et il n\u2019\xe9tait pas couvert. C\u2019est parce qu\u2019il perdait de l\u2019eau et devenait insalubre qu\u2019il fut r\xe9par\xe9 et transform\xe9 pour le mettre dans le sens actuel et le couvrir d\u2019un toit d\xe9bordant, prot\xe9geant aussi les usagers des intemp\xe9ries. Sa version \xab finale \xbb serait ainsi dat\xe9e \xe0 1875.","- Les lavoirs ont longtemps mal port\xe9 leur nom. Ils auraient pu s\u2019appeler \xab les rin\xe7oirs \xbb car au d\xe9part ils ne servaient qu\u2019\xe0 rincer le linge et non \xe0 le laver. Le lavage se faisait chez l\u2019habitant ou dans la cour des fermes. On laisser tremper le linge et les v\xeatements plusieurs jours dans des bacs d\u2019eau ti\xe8de m\xe9lang\xe9e le plus souvent \xe0 de la cendre (riche en carbonate de potassium, mol\xe9cule au pouvoir nettoyant) avant d\u2019aller rincer tout \xe7a au lavoir. C\u2019est la g\xe9n\xe9ralisation du savon, devenu financi\xe8rement accessible au plus grand nombre \xe0 la fin du XIX\xe8me, qui a permis de \xab transporter \xbb l\u2019op\xe9ration de lavage au lavoir.","- Les lavoirs \xe9taient r\xe9serv\xe9s aux femmes : un homme pouvait m\xeame risquer une amende en s\u2019y rendant !!! D\u2019ailleurs, les surnoms populaires attribu\xe9s aux lavoirs sont tr\xe8s sexistes : \xab parloirs des femmes \xbb, \xab h\xf4tel des bavardages \xbb, \xab radio-lavoirs \xbb ou encore \xab moulins \xe0 paroles \xbb. Ils \xe9taient des lieux de vie important au village o\xf9 les femmes bavardaient pendant leur dur labeur, en commentant les derni\xe8res actualit\xe9s, en disant ce qu\u2019elles savaient\u2026 ou ce qu\u2019elles ne savaient pas d\u2019ailleurs\u2026 Les fameux \xab cancans \xbb qui donn\xe8rent le verbe \xab cancaner \xbb mais ceci est une autre histoire\u2026","\u2013 Enfin, c\u2019est une pand\xe9mie (celle du chol\xe9ra de 1832\u20131834) qui a conduit \xe0 construire massivement des lavoirs un peu partout en France, afin d\u2019am\xe9liorer l\u2019hygi\xe8ne g\xe9n\xe9rale de la population et d\u2019essayer de stopper la transmission des maladies en \xe9vitant le rin\xe7age du linge directement dans les cours d\u2019eau (sources, mares, rivi\xe8res, fleuves,\u2026). L\u2019arriv\xe9e de la machine \xe0 laver dans les foyers (\xe0 partir de 1950) signa h\xe9las la fin des lavoirs qui restent n\xe9anmoins aujourd\u2019hui des lieux quasi \xab m\xe9moriels \xbb, car ils ont \xe9t\xe9 les t\xe9moins discrets de petits r\xe9cits et grandes discussions de nos anc\xeatres maternelles sur plusieurs si\xe8cles\u2026","Vous \xeates presque arriver au bout de votre aventure. Je tiens tout d\u2019abord \xe0 vous f\xe9liciter pour votre parcours et je vous propose une halte au restaurant qui se trouve devant vous. Dans ce restaurant vous pourrez appr\xe9cier une cuisine cr\xe9ative avec des ingr\xe9dients locaux, une s\xe9lection vari\xe9e de vins et une ambiance accueillante.","Vous pourrez aussi tout simplement vous d\xe9salt\xe9rer en buvant une boisson fra\xeeche au c\u0153ur de la rue pi\xe9tonne de Tr\xe9voux. Ils couronnerons votre journ\xe9e d'exploration avec une exp\xe9rience culinaire m\xe9morable.","Vous voici devant l'\xe9glise Saint-Symphorien, l'\xe9difice religieux principal de Tr\xe9voux. Cette belle \xe9glise de style n\xe9o-roman a remplac\xe9 une premi\xe8re \xe9glise \xe9difi\xe9e au XIVe si\xe8cle qui avait \xe9t\xe9 \xe9lev\xe9e au rang de coll\xe9giale en 1523, t\xe9moignant de l'importance religieuse de Tr\xe9voux \xe0 l'\xe9poque.","Devenue inadapt\xe9e \xe0 l'expansion de la ville, elle fut remplac\xe9e par l'\xe9difice actuel dont les travaux d\xe9but\xe8rent en mars 1899 sous la direction des architectes lyonnais Louis Antoine Bresson puis de Tony Bourbon apr\xe8s le d\xe9c\xe8s du premier en 1893. Elle fut inaugur\xe9e en 1904 apr\xe8s cinq ann\xe9es de construction men\xe9es par des artisans locaux, Auguste Chambon et Baptiste Faugeron.","Con\xe7ue selon un plan en croix latine, l'\xe9glise pr\xe9sente une particularit\xe9 : faute de place sur ce terrain pentu, elle n'a pas pu \xeatre orient\xe9e selon la tradition. C'est donc le ch\u0153ur qui regarde vers l'ouest, et l'entr\xe9e vers l'est - l'inverse de la grande majorit\xe9 des \xe9glises catholiques !","La configuration du terrain en pente a entrain\xe9 des surco\xfbts consid\xe9rables pour stabiliser les fondations, r\xe9sultat = pas de clocher, ou plut\xf4t un clocher provisoire en bois qui patiente toujours dans le jardin du presbyt\xe8re ! Sa position sur l'escarpement lui donne n\xe9anmoins une allure majestueuse qui domine la Sa\xf4ne. L'\xe9glise a \xe9t\xe9 \xe9difi\xe9e \xe0 l'emplacement de l'ancienne \xe9glise-forteresse qui d\xe9fendait autrefois la Porte de Lyon, sur le c\xf4t\xe9 est de la place o\xf9 se trouve le Parlement.","Saint Symphorien \xe9tait un jeune martyr chr\xe9tien n\xe9 vers 159 \xe0 Autun, mort vers 179 sous le r\xe8gne de Marc Aur\xe8le. Un jour, alors que la statue de la d\xe9esse Cyb\xe8le \xe9tait promen\xe9e dans les rues d'Autun pour \xeatre v\xe9n\xe9r\xe9e, Symphorien refuse de l'honorer et se moque m\xeame du cort\xe8ge. Arr\xeat\xe9 et interrog\xe9 par le gouverneur romain, il affirme qu'en tant que chr\xe9tien il n'adore que le vrai Dieu, ce qui lui vaut d'\xeatre d\xe9capit\xe9 \xe0 l'\xe2ge de 20 ans. \xc0 l'\xe9poque m\xe9rovingienne, il \xe9tait consid\xe9r\xe9 comme un saint national, d'o\xf9 le grand nombre d'\xe9glises qui lui sont d\xe9di\xe9es en France !","Le style n\xe9o-roman de cette \xe9glise correspond \xe0 un mouvement architectural du XIXe si\xe8cle qui cherchait \xe0 retrouver la grandeur de l'art roman m\xe9di\xe9val. Les caract\xe9ristiques distinctives les plus couramment employ\xe9es dans les b\xe2timents n\xe9o-romans sont les vo\xfbtes en berceau, les fen\xeatres en arc plein cintre et les bandeaux. Ce style \xe9tait particuli\xe8rement appr\xe9ci\xe9 pour les \xe9difices religieux car il \xe9voquait la spiritualit\xe9 et la solidit\xe9 des grandes abbayes du Moyen \xc2ge, tout en permettant l'usage de techniques de construction modernes.","Les \xe9glises du d\xe9but du XXe si\xe8cle t\xe9moignent souvent des difficult\xe9s financi\xe8res des communes de l'\xe9poque ! Entre les co\xfbts de construction, les contraintes du terrain et les impr\xe9vus, beaucoup d'\xe9glises de cette p\xe9riode ont d\xfb faire des compromis. Certaines sont rest\xe9es inachev\xe9es, d'autres ont vu leurs projets de clochers report\xe9s aux calendes grecques... Comme ici \xe0 Tr\xe9voux o\xf9 le clocher provisoire en bois attend toujours dans le jardin du presbyt\xe8re depuis plus d'un si\xe8cle ! Ces \"imperfections\" font aujourd'hui tout le charme et l'authenticit\xe9 de ces \xe9difices qui racontent aussi l'histoire \xe9conomique et sociale de nos villes.","Quelques r\xe8gles avant votre d\xe9part...","Veillez \xe0 ne pas d\xe9grader les monuments, les b\xe2timents ainsi que les QR codes et tout autre \xe9l\xe9ment essentiel au bon fonctionnement de l'application. Le patrimoine de Tr\xe9voux est pr\xe9cieux ; sans lui, la d\xe9couverte de la ville perdrait tout son sens.","Nous vous conseillons de suivre les itin\xe9raires propos\xe9s pour assurer votre s\xe9curit\xe9 et vous permettre de d\xe9couvrir les plus beaux endroits de Tr\xe9voux. Ces parcours ont \xe9t\xe9 choisis sp\xe9cialement pour vous permettre la meilleure exp\xe9rience possible.","Votre s\xe9curit\xe9 est de votre responsabilit\xe9. Soyez vigilant(e) \xe0 la circulation et aux autres dangers potentiels. La mairie de Tr\xe9voux d\xe9cline toute responsabilit\xe9 en cas d'accident.","Pour profiter pleinement des informations audios, r\xe9glez le volume sonore de votre t\xe9l\xe9phone \xe0 un niveau suffisant pour vous permettre une bonne \xe9coute tout en profitant de la beaut\xe9 des lieux.","Pour une exp\xe9rience optimale, la plupart des lieux \xe0 d\xe9couvrir se d\xe9clenchent automatiquement une fois que vous atteignez l'endroit indiqu\xe9 par l'itin\xe9raire. Il est donc n\xe9cessaire d'autoriser l'acc\xe8s \xe0 la localisation de votre appareil.","Ne laissez aucun d\xe9chet derri\xe8re vous et respectez la nature et les espaces verts pour pr\xe9server la beaut\xe9 de Tr\xe9voux qui s\u2019offre \xe0 vous.","Soyez courtois(e) et respectueux(se) envers les habitants de Tr\xe9voux. N'h\xe9sitez pas \xe0 leur demander des informations ou des conseils, ils seront ravis de vous aider.","Assurez-vous que votre t\xe9l\xe9phone est suffisamment charg\xe9 avant de commencer votre visite. Vous pouvez \xe9galement emporter une batterie externe pour \xe9viter les interruptions.","Apr\xe8s votre visite, n'h\xe9sitez pas \xe0 nous faire part de vos commentaires et suggestions pour am\xe9liorer l'application et les parcours de visite.","Vous passez d\xe9sormais sous la porte de Villars, seul vestige des anciennes fortifications de Tr\xe9voux ! Cette porte m\xe9di\xe9vale, post\xe9e au nord-est, est la derni\xe8re survivante des quatre portes qui permettaient autrefois d'entrer dans la ville fortifi\xe9e. Les trois autres - la porte de Lyon \xe0 l'est, la porte de Sa\xf4ne au sud et la porte de Saint-Bernard \xe0 l'ouest - ont malheureusement disparu au fil des si\xe8cles.","Construite en pierre dor\xe9e et brique, cette porte \xe9tait int\xe9gr\xe9e dans le rempart qui encerclait enti\xe8rement la cit\xe9 \xe0 l'\xe9poque de la Principaut\xe9 de Dombes. Elle tire son nom des sires de Villars, qui dominaient la r\xe9gion d\xe8s le XIIe si\xe8cle avant de s'unir aux sires de Thoire - donnant la lign\xe9e des Thoire-Villars, qui vendirent finalement le fief aux Bourbon en 1402.","Ces fortifications n'\xe9taient pas qu'un symbole : elles r\xe9pondaient \xe0 une n\xe9cessit\xe9 militaire r\xe9elle. Les attaques r\xe9p\xe9t\xe9es de la Savoie et de la Bourgogne justifiaient cette protection. Chaque porte \xe9tait surveill\xe9e, contr\xf4l\xe9e, et ferm\xe9e la nuit. Passer cette porte, c'\xe9tait entrer dans une principaut\xe9 souveraine, avec ses propres lois et sa propre monnaie ! Aujourd'hui, elle nous rappelle que Tr\xe9voux fut bien plus qu'une simple bourgade : une v\xe9ritable cit\xe9-\xc9tat au c\u0153ur de l'Europe m\xe9di\xe9vale.","Les portes de ville au Moyen \xc2ge \xe9taient bien plus que de simples ouvertures dans les remparts ! Elles constituaient de v\xe9ritables postes de contr\xf4le o\xf9 s'exer\xe7aient les droits seigneuriaux. Les gardes v\xe9rifiaient l'identit\xe9 des voyageurs, percevaient les taxes d'entr\xe9e et contr\xf4laient les marchandises. Chaque porte avait ses horaires : ouverture \xe0 l'aube, fermeture au coucher du soleil. Arriver de nuit signifiait dormir dehors ! Ces portes \xe9taient souvent flanqu\xe9es de tours et \xe9quip\xe9es de herses, ponts-levis et meurtri\xe8res. Elles marquaient la fronti\xe8re entre le monde ext\xe9rieur et l'espace urbain prot\xe9g\xe9.","La construction des remparts \xe9tait un investissement colossal pour les villes m\xe9di\xe9vales ! Il fallait mobiliser des centaines d'ouvriers pendant des ann\xe9es, extraire et transporter des milliers de tonnes de pierre, organiser des corv\xe9es pour les habitants. \xc0 Tr\xe9voux, le rempart combinait brique et pierre selon une technique r\xe9pandue dans la r\xe9gion. Ces fortifications pesaient lourd dans les finances municipales, des ann\xe9es durant ! Mais c'\xe9tait vital : une ville non fortifi\xe9e \xe9tait \xe0 la merci du premier seigneur de guerre venu. Les remparts \xe9taient donc un gage de prosp\xe9rit\xe9 et d'ind\xe9pendance.","Le nom des portes \xe9tait choisi avec soin et r\xe9v\xe9lait l'organisation g\xe9ographique de l'\xe9poque ! La porte de Lyon menait vers cette grande cit\xe9, la porte de Sa\xf4ne vers la rivi\xe8re, la porte de Saint-Bernard vers ce bourg voisin. Cette d\xe9nomination permettait aux voyageurs de s'orienter facilement : \"Prenez la porte de Lyon si vous voulez rejoindre la grande route du sud !\". Ces noms sont rest\xe9s dans la m\xe9moire collective et donnent encore aujourd'hui leurs appellations \xe0 des rues, places ou quartiers. Ils racontent l'histoire des \xe9changes commerciaux et des relations entre les territoires \xe0 l'\xe9poque m\xe9di\xe9vale.","Quitter la visite ?","Ta progression sur ce parcours ne sera pas sauvegard\xe9e. Tu devras recommencer cette \xe9tape si tu reviens plus tard.","Quitter la visite","Continuer la visite","Vous n'\xeates pas au point de d\xe9part","Vous semblez loin du point de d\xe9part de cette \xe9tape. Voulez-vous un itin\xe9raire pour vous y rendre ?","M'y rendre","Continuer sans itin\xe9raire","Rejoindre le d\xe9part","Impossible de calculer l'itin\xe9raire pour le moment.","\xc0 pied","En voiture","\xc0 v\xe9lo",u.H,"D'accord","Recentrer","Bravo, vous avez termin\xe9 la visite !","Vous avez parcouru le c\u0153ur historique de Tr\xe9voux et d\xe9couvert son riche patrimoine. Merci d'avoir particip\xe9 \xe0 cette visite !","{distance} parcourus \xe0 pied","Je viens de terminer la visite de Tr\xe9voux ! \ud83c\udff0\ud83d\udeb6","Partager","Voir mon carnet de voyage","\xc0 d\xe9couvrir","Tes photos souvenirs","R\xe9compenses","Tes badges gagn\xe9s","Voir mes r\xe9compenses","Retour \xe0 l'accueil","N","Localisation requise","Cette fonctionnalit\xe9 a besoin de conna\xeetre ta position pour te guider et d\xe9tecter ton arriv\xe9e. Autorise l'acc\xe8s \xe0 la localisation pour continuer.","L'acc\xe8s \xe0 la localisation a \xe9t\xe9 refus\xe9. Ouvre les r\xe9glages de l'app pour l'activer, puis reviens ici.","La localisation (GPS) est d\xe9sactiv\xe9e sur ton t\xe9l\xe9phone. Active-la dans les r\xe9glages pour continuer.","Autoriser la localisation","Ouvrir les r\xe9glages de l'app","Activer la localisation","Plus tard","En choisissant \xab Plus tard \xbb, tu quitteras la visite en cours : la localisation est indispensable pour continuer le parcours.","Mise \xe0 jour requise","Une nouvelle version de l'application est disponible et doit \xeatre install\xe9e pour continuer.","Mettre \xe0 jour","Informations l\xe9gales","Mentions l\xe9gales","CGU","Confidentialit\xe9","La version de r\xe9f\xe9rence de cette politique est disponible en ligne :","Consulter en ligne","Fermer","Informations l\xe9gales","S","O","E","\ud83c\udf33 Le Ch\xeane du Sage","Bienvenue, jeune apprenti chevalier ! On raconte qu'ici se dressait un ch\xeane centenaire, t\xe9moin de la naissance du ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux. Nul ne sait si cette l\xe9gende est vraie, mais les anciens disaient que ses racines gardaient les secrets de notre histoire.","Combien de branches principales ce ch\xeane majestueux poss\xe8de-t-il ?","Entre 3 et 4 branches","Entre 5 et 7 branches","Entre 8 et 10 branches","Plus de 10 branches","Regardez bien vers le sommet de l'arbre, comptez seulement les plus grosses branches qui partent du tronc principal.","\ud83d\udc41\ufe0f La Pierre du Guetteur","La l\xe9gende raconte qu'une pierre ancienne servait ici de poste de guet aux gardes du ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux, qui surveillaient la Sa\xf4ne et les chemins menant \xe0 la forteresse. Comme beaucoup de chevaliers de l'\xe9poque, ils utilisaient leurs propres codes et symboles pour se reconna\xeetre.","Que gravaient principalement les chevaliers sur leurs boucliers pour se distinguer au combat ?","Des \xe9p\xe9es crois\xe9es","Leurs blasons familiaux","Des tours de ch\xe2teau","Des fleurs de lys royales","Chaque famille noble avait ses propres couleurs et symboles h\xe9r\xe9ditaires pour se faire reconna\xeetre.","\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f L'Arbre aux \xc9cussons","On raconte qu'un vieil arbre de cette for\xeat portait autrefois des \xe9cussons sculpt\xe9s dans son \xe9corce, en m\xe9moire des seigneurs de Tr\xe9voux. Comme tous les nobles, ceux-ci poss\xe9daient leurs propres armoiries, qui ornaient boucliers, banni\xe8res et murs du ch\xe2teau.","Quelles \xe9taient les couleurs traditionnelles les plus nobles utilis\xe9es dans les blasons m\xe9di\xe9vaux ?","Rouge et or (or jaune)","Bleu et argent (blanc)","Vert et violet","Noir et blanc uniquement","Les m\xe9taux pr\xe9cieux (or et argent) \xe9taient consid\xe9r\xe9s comme les couleurs les plus nobles en h\xe9raldique.","\ud83c\udf3f Le Bosquet des Herboristes","Selon la l\xe9gende, les moines du ch\xe2teau seraient venus cultiver ici un jardin de simples, ces plantes m\xe9dicinales si pr\xe9cieuses au Moyen \xc2ge. Leur savoir en botanique aurait \xe9t\xe9 immense, soignant les habitants de Tr\xe9voux gr\xe2ce \xe0 des rem\xe8des naturels.","Quelle plante \xe9tait particuli\xe8rement r\xe9put\xe9e au Moyen \xc2ge pour soigner les maux de t\xeate et am\xe9liorer la m\xe9moire ?","La menthe fra\xeeche","Le thym sauvage","La sauge officinale","Toutes ces plantes","Les moines connaissaient bien les vertus de nombreuses plantes aromatiques de nos r\xe9gions.","\ud83d\udc8e La Clairi\xe8re du Tr\xe9sor","F\xe9licitations, brave chevalier ! Tu viens de traverser la clairi\xe8re secr\xe8te des gardiens de la for\xeat de Tr\xe9voux, du moins telle que la l\xe9gende la raconte. Ici s'ach\xe8ve ton parcours, mais rappelle-toi que la v\xe9ritable aventure ne fait que commencer quand on part \xe0 la d\xe9couverte de notre patrimoine.","Selon la sagesse des anciens chevaliers, quel est le plus grand tr\xe9sor qu'un h\xe9ros peut d\xe9couvrir ?","Un coffre rempli d'or","Une \xe9p\xe9e magique","La connaissance et la sagesse","Un parchemin aux secrets","Les vrais h\xe9ros savent que la richesse la plus pr\xe9cieuse ne se mesure pas en pi\xe8ces d'or.","Badge du Sage","Badge du Guetteur","Badge des \xc9cussons","Badge de l'Herboriste","Badge du Tr\xe9sor","La Carte de la For\xeat","Voir mon tr\xe9sor","Le Ch\xeane des Secrets","Jeu de m\xe9moire","Sous ses vieilles racines, le Ch\xeane cache des paires de secrets. Retrouve-les toutes pour gagner sa confiance !","La Pierre du Guetteur","\xc9nigmes de la for\xeat","Le Guetteur veille sur la for\xeat depuis toujours. R\xe9ponds \xe0 ses \xe9nigmes pour prouver ta sagesse.","Je souffle sans jamais me voir, je fais danser les feuilles et voyager les graines. Qui suis-je ?","La pluie","Le vent","Le soleil","La rivi\xe8re","Je porte ma maison sur mon dos et je laisse un chemin brillant derri\xe8re moi. Qui suis-je ?","Le h\xe9risson","La limace","L'escargot","Le l\xe9zard","Plus je vieillis, plus je grandis. Mes bras touchent le ciel et mes pieds boivent la terre. Qui suis-je ?","L'arbre","La rivi\xe8re","La montagne","Le nuage","L'Arbre aux \xc9cussons","Jeu de rythme","Observe bien le passage des gardiens de la for\xeat, puis rejoue leur ronde dans le bon ordre.","Le Bosquet des Herboristes","Jeu de tri","Un lutin farceur a m\xe9lang\xe9 son tr\xe9sor \xe0 ses farces ! Aide l'Herboriste \xe0 trier le vrai du faux.","Vrai tr\xe9sor","Farce de lutin","Une fraise des bois","Une myrtille","Une ch\xe2taigne","Un masque de farceur","Un jeu de cartes truqu\xe9","Une boule de verre","La Clairi\xe8re du Tr\xe9sor","\xc9preuve finale","Le coffre s'est bris\xe9 en morceaux ! Touche deux pi\xe8ces pour les \xe9changer et reconstitue l'image du tr\xe9sor.","Quitter la qu\xeate ?","Ta progression est d\xe9j\xe0 enregistr\xe9e, mais ce mini-jeu recommencera si tu reviens.","Quitter","Continuer \xe0 jouer","Continuer","Badge obtenu !","Pas tout \xe0 fait... essaie encore !","{count} coups","Observe bien...","\xc0 toi de jouer !","La Chasse en For\xeat","Bienvenue, jeune aventurier ! Je suis le gardien de cette for\xeat enchant\xe9e. Explore mes 5 clairi\xe8res, r\xe9sous leurs \xe9preuves, et d\xe9couvre le tr\xe9sor cach\xe9 au bout du chemin !","Commencer l'aventure","Clique sur la premi\xe8re clairi\xe8re pour commencer !","Continue vers la prochaine clairi\xe8re !","Bravo, aventurier ! Toutes les clairi\xe8res sont explor\xe9es, va chercher ton tr\xe9sor !","Tu es \xe0 mi-chemin, continue comme \xe7a !","Bravo ! Manche suivante !","Encore un effort, derni\xe8re manche !","Passer cette activit\xe9","Bienvenue dans la for\xeat de Tr\xe9voux ! On y raconte de vieilles l\xe9gendes, transmises de g\xe9n\xe9ration en g\xe9n\xe9ration. Personne ne sait ce qui est vrai, mais elles m\xe9ritent d'\xeatre cont\xe9es. D\xe9couvre-les, chapitre apr\xe8s chapitre.","Commencer la qu\xeate","Temps restant : "," \xe9tapes","Pr\xeat(e) \xe0 d\xe9couvrir la suite de la l\xe9gende ?","D\xe9couvrir ce chapitre","R\xe9initialiser la qu\xeate","Besoin d'un indice ?","Bravo ! Bonne r\xe9ponse !","Essayez encore ! Utilisez l'indice si n\xe9cessaire.","Un nouveau chapitre t'attend !","Contenu en fran\xe7ais","La chasse en for\xeat n'est disponible qu'en fran\xe7ais pour le moment (texte et audio). Tu peux quand m\xeame y acc\xe9der, ou passer cette \xe9tape.","Acc\xe9der quand m\xeame","Passer","La For\xeat Enchant\xe9e","Quitter la visite ?","\xcates-vous s\xfbr de vouloir quitter la visite ?","Annuler","Quitter","Passer la qu\xeate","Passer la chasse en for\xeat ?","Tu pourras toujours y revenir une prochaine fois. Passer quand m\xeame ?","Oui, passer","Non, continuer la qu\xeate","F\xe9licitations, Chevalier !","Vous avez brillamment accompli la Qu\xeate des Gardiens de la For\xeat de Tr\xe9voux ! Votre courage et votre sagesse vous ont men\xe9 \xe0 la victoire.","Temps \xe9coul\xe9 !","Le temps imparti pour votre qu\xeate est \xe9coul\xe9, mais ne vous d\xe9couragez pas ! Chaque aventure est une occasion d'apprendre. Vous pouvez recommencer pour am\xe9liorer votre score !"," \xe9tapes accomplies sur "," badges obtenus","Aucun badge collect\xe9 cette fois-ci.\nRecommencez pour tenter votre chance !","Recommencer la qu\xeate","Continuer la visite","Partager mon dipl\xf4me","J'ai relev\xe9 le d\xe9fi de la Qu\xeate des Gardiens de la For\xeat de Tr\xe9voux ! \ud83c\udfc6\ud83c\udf33","Votre avis compte pour nous !","Vous venez de terminer votre visite. Un avis sur le store nous aide \xe9norm\xe9ment \xe0 am\xe9liorer l'application et \xe0 la faire conna\xeetre autour de vous.","Donner mon avis","Plus tard","Bient\xf4t disponible !",u.H,"D'accord","Bient\xf4t\ndisponible","Nos lieux","Nos lieux","Parcours","Liste","Carte","Voir la fiche compl\xe8te","Destination atteinte !","Vous \xeates arriv\xe9 \xe0 {place}. Pr\xeat \xe0 d\xe9couvrir ce lieu ?","D\xe9couvrir le lieu","M'y rendre","Navigation en cours\u2026","Donne ton avis","Je recommande","Pas pour moi","Un commentaire ? (facultatif)","Envoyer","Merci pour ton avis !","Ton commentaire sera visible apr\xe8s une br\xe8ve v\xe9rification.","Fermer","Impossible d'envoyer ton avis pour le moment.","Ce commentaire ne peut pas \xeatre envoy\xe9 tel quel.","Signaler un probl\xe8me","Signaler un probl\xe8me","Quel est le probl\xe8me ?","QR code illisible ou cass\xe9","Le GPS ne se d\xe9clenche pas","Probl\xe8me avec l'audio-guide","Erreur dans un texte ou une photo","Autre","D\xe9crivez le probl\xe8me (facultatif)","Envoyer le signalement","Signalement envoy\xe9","Merci, nous allons regarder \xe7a rapidement.","\xc9chec de l'envoi. V\xe9rifiez votre connexion et r\xe9essayez.","R\xe9essayer","Fermer","Avis","{percent}% des visiteurs recommandent","Sois le premier \xe0 donner ton avis !","D\xe9j\xe0 des avis sur ce lieu !","Donner mon avis","Tu as d\xe9j\xe0 donn\xe9 ton avis sur ce lieu",u.u,"Visitez cette belle \xe9glise gothique et d\xe9couvrez son riche patrimoine artistique et spirituel.","Admirez cette tour historique qui domine la ville et tr\xf4ne fi\xe8rement au c\u0153ur de la cit\xe9.","Profitez d'un panorama exceptionnel sur la vall\xe9e de la Sa\xf4ne et les monts du Beaujolais.","Franchissez cette porte m\xe9di\xe9vale, vestige des anciennes fortifications de la ville.","Plongez dans l'histoire du patrimoine local avec ce magnifique lavoir restaur\xe9 du XIXe si\xe8cle.","Profitez d'une halte dans ce magnifique parlement des Dombes et de ses superbes fresques.","D\xe9couvrez cette rue embl\xe9matique de Tr\xe9voux et ses ateliers artistiques.","Audio-guide","Audio-guide disponible","Audio-guide non disponible dans votre langue","Je suis arriv\xe9(e) ?","V\xe9rification de la position","Il semble que vous soyez encore \xe0 {distance} du lieu. Rapprochez-vous, ou confirmez si vous \xeates bien arriv\xe9(e).","Impossible de v\xe9rifier ta position pour le moment (signal GPS indisponible). Tu peux r\xe9essayer, ou continuer si tu es bien arriv\xe9(e).","Continuer quand m\xeame","R\xe9essayer","Envie de vivre toute la visite ?","T\xe9l\xe9charge l'application Tr\xe9voux pour suivre le parcours complet, d\xe9bloquer les d\xe9fis et bien plus.","T\xe9l\xe9charger sur Android","T\xe9l\xe9charger sur iPhone","\xc0 propos","Galerie photo","Scanner un QR code","Scanner","Scannez le QR code d'un lieu pour y acc\xe9der directement","QR Code non reconnu","Scan annul\xe9","Prochaine \xe9tape","Dur\xe9e de l'\xe9tape : ","Dur\xe9e totale restante : "," min","Continuer","La For\xeat Enchant\xe9e","Fin du parcours","Reprendre votre visite ?","Vous avez un parcours en cours. Voulez-vous reprendre o\xf9 vous en \xe9tiez, ou recommencer \xe0 z\xe9ro ?","Reprendre","Recommencer","Vous \xeates \xe0 Tr\xe9voux !","Profitez-en pour d\xe9couvrir la ville avec notre parcours guid\xe9.","D\xe9couvrir maintenant","Plus tard","Carnet de voyage","Mon carnet de voyage","Une photo souvenir \xe0 chaque lieu visit\xe9 \u2014 appuie sur l'appareil photo pour en ajouter une.","Badges de la for\xeat","Prendre une photo","Choisir dans la galerie","Supprimer la photo ?","Cette photo souvenir sera d\xe9finitivement supprim\xe9e du carnet de voyage.","Supprimer","Annuler","Partager mon certificat","Mon carnet de voyage \xe0 Tr\xe9voux","Un souvenir de votre passage dans la ville","Partager mon carnet","T\xe9l\xe9charger","Ton souvenir de Tr\xe9voux","Carnet de voyage","Tr\xe9voux","V\xe9cu avec Flan\xe9a, l'appli qui fait d\xe9couvrir Tr\xe9voux autrement.","Image enregistr\xe9e dans la galerie !","Impossible d'enregistrer l'image.","G\xe9n\xe9ration de l'image...","Immortalise ce moment !","Prends une photo souvenir de ce lieu : elle reste dans l'application, ajout\xe9e \xe0 ton carnet de voyage personnel. Tu peux la consulter \xe0 tout moment, et t\xe9l\xe9charger le carnet complet \xe0 la fin du parcours.","Prendre une photo","Plus tard","Coup de c\u0153ur","Combien de bassins vois-tu dans le lavoir ?","Regarde bien \xe0 l'int\xe9rieur, ils sont c\xf4te \xe0 c\xf4te.","Bravo, tu as l'\u0153il !","Combien d'\xe9tages compte la tour de l'horloge ?","L\xe8ve les yeux et compte les niveaux, du bas jusqu'en haut.","Exact, quel bon observateur !","Vrai ou faux : un ch\xeane peut vivre plus de 100 ans.","Pense \xe0 la taille et \xe0 l'\xe2ge des plus grands arbres que tu connais.","Bien jou\xe9, petit naturaliste !","Quelle forme a l'ouverture de la porte ?","Ronde, en arc","Carr\xe9e","En triangle","Regarde le haut de l'ouverture : est-il droit ou courb\xe9 ?","Bravo, bien vu !","Combien de tours vois-tu sur le ch\xe2teau ?","Fais le tour du regard sans bouger les pieds.","Super, tu as tout rep\xe9r\xe9 !","Que vois-tu \xe0 l'horizon depuis ce point de vue ?","Regarde bien loin, au-del\xe0 des toits.","Magnifique, tu as le sens de l'observation !","Quel symbole vois-tu sur la fa\xe7ade de l'\xe9glise ?","Une croix","Une \xe9toile","Un blason","Regarde tout en haut, au centre de la fa\xe7ade.","Bien vu, champion !","Cr\xe9e ton h\xe9ros !","Comment tu t'appelles ?","Ton pr\xe9nom","Choisis ton avatar","Chevalier","Princesse","Explorateur","Magicien","Salut {name} !","pi\xe8ces de puzzle","Continuer l'aventure","Bravo, tu as termin\xe9 toutes les \xe9tapes !","Verrouill\xe9","En cours","Termin\xe9","Un indice ?","Passer","Passer ce d\xe9fi ?","Tu pourras toujours r\xe9essayer une prochaine fois. Passer quand m\xeame ?","Oui, passer","Non, je r\xe9essaie","Presque ! Essaie encore \ud83d\udcaa","Vrai","Faux","Valider","Nouvelle pi\xe8ce de puzzle !","Relever le d\xe9fi !","Tu y es presque, continue !","F\xe9licitations, {name} !","Tu as termin\xe9 le Parcours ludique de Tr\xe9voux avec brio !","Dipl\xf4me d'aventurier","certifie que {name} a explor\xe9 les secrets de Tr\xe9voux et relev\xe9 tous les d\xe9fis du Parcours ludique.","J'ai termin\xe9 le Parcours ludique de Tr\xe9voux avec {name} ! \ud83c\udfc6\ud83e\udde9","Partager","Gratte l'\xe9cran avec le doigt pour r\xe9v\xe9ler ton puzzle !","Tout d\xe9voiler","Retour \xe0 l'accueil","Tourner la roue de r\xe9compense","Roue de r\xe9compense bient\xf4t disponible","Parcours ludique","Dur\xe9e","\xc2ge conseill\xe9","Niveau physique","Pour qui ?","Annuler","Voici le parcours","Un carnet de voyage \xe0 cr\xe9er","Pendant la visite, l'application te proposera de prendre une photo \xe0 chaque lieu. Elle reste dans l'application, ajout\xe9e \xe0 ton carnet de voyage personnel : consultable \xe0 tout moment, et t\xe9l\xe9chargeable \xe0 la fin du parcours.","Parcours non accessible aux poussettes.","Environ 1h30 \xe0 2h","D\xe8s 12 ans conseill\xe9",u.Z,"Tout public","D\xe9couvrez les tr\xe9sors cach\xe9s de Tr\xe9voux au fil d'une balade guid\xe9e : ch\xe2teau, tour de l'horloge, lavoir et bien d'autres surprises, \xe0 votre rythme.","Environ 1h30 \xe0 2h","D\xe8s 6 ans",u.Z,"En famille, avec les enfants","Vivez le parcours culturel en mode jeu ! Ton h\xe9ros rel\xe8ve un d\xe9fi \xe0 chaque lieu, r\xe9colte des pi\xe8ces de puzzle, et re\xe7oit un dipl\xf4me \xe0 la fin de l'aventure."],t.l)
B.Lg=new A.bp(B.eP,["trevouxapp","Home","Scan QR","Our Places","Continue","Let's go!","Start Guidance","Continue","Are you ready?","The adventure begins in...","Cultural route","Forest hunt","Trophies","My progress","Your visited places and journey trophies","Visited places"," places visited out of ","Journeys & trophies","Locked","Unlocked!","Try my luck","See my prize","Coming soon","Spin the wheel!","Spin the wheel","Congratulations!","Your code","Show this code to a partner business to claim your prize.","Prize already claimed","-10% at a partner restaurant","A free drink","A free dessert","-5% at a partner shop","A surprise souvenir","Try again next time","Got it","Only one spin per device per day. Try again tomorrow!","The reward wheel isn't available right now.","Couldn't spin the wheel right now. Check your connection and try again.","Did you know?","Discover the Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","A stroll along the Sa\xf4ne","The Saturday morning market","Dear travelers, welcome to Tr\xe9voux! You're about to discover the secrets and history of this wonderful medieval town.","Let's go!","Before starting your journey, please select your route.","Cultural route","Fun route","One last thing.. What's your mode of transportation?","I'm on a bike","I'm in a car","I'm on foot","\ud83c\udff0 Quest of the Guardians\nof the Tr\xe9voux Forest","\u23f1\ufe0f Time remaining: 15:00","\ud83d\udcc8 Your progress","0/5","\ud83c\udfc5 Badge collection","\ud83d\ude80 Start the Adventure","\ud83d\udcf1 Scan the QR Code","\ud83d\udd04 Try again","Step title","Step description","\ud83c\udfa7 Listen to the story","\ud83d\udca1 hint","\ud83d\udca1 Hint appears here","Discover the history of Tr\xe9voux through this interactive adventure! \ud83c\udf1f","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Orme Panorama","Rue des Arts","The Former Parliament of Dombes","The Tr\xe9voux Wash House","The Clock Tower","The Church","The Villars Gate","Go visit","Photo preview","The Ch\xe2teau","Discover the iconic Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux, a witness to the history of the Dombes and former seat of its parliament.","\ud83e\udded Start navigation","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux","Scan and Discover","\ud83c\udfc6 Congratulations, Knight!","Congratulatory message","\ud83d\udcca Your Stats","Quest statistics","\ud83d\udcdc Your Certificate","\ud83d\udcbe Download the Certificate","\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Badges Earned","\ud83d\udcf1 Share my Results","\ud83d\udd04 Restart the Quest","Continue the tour","Thank you for taking part in this adventure in the Tr\xe9voux forest!","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","Next step","Step duration: 10 minutes","Total time remaining: 30 minutes","Continue","The Ch\xe2teau","Dear travelers, you are about to step into the heart of Tr\xe9voux's history by discovering its medieval ch\xe2teau. Overlooking the town and the Sa\xf4ne, this iconic building bears witness to the prestigious past of the former capital of the Principality of Dombes.","Before reaching its ramparts, let yourself be charmed by a pleasant walk through the picturesque streets of the old town. Once there, enjoy an exceptional panorama and immerse yourself in the fascinating stories of this history-laden place. Get ready for a journey through time where every stone tells a story!","Start navigation","Navigation2","Open navigation drawer","Close navigation drawer","Android Studio","android.studio@android.com","Navigation header","Settings","Home","Gallery","Slideshow","MapsActivity","You are now standing before the Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux, a symbol of power and witness to five centuries of extraordinary history! This fortified castle was built around 1300 by the Lords of Thoire-Villars to oversee the port and the toll on the Sa\xf4ne. But everything changed in 1402: the last of the Thoire-Villars line sold the fief to Louis II de Bourbon, giving birth to one of the most fascinating principalities in Europe.","Built in two main phases during the 14th century, this stone fortress is an imposing building, listed as a Historic Monument since 1913. Its unique octagonal keep, decorated with golden and white stones, once rose to 28 meters \u2014 today reduced to 16 meters following the Revolution \u2014 and still offers an exceptional panorama over the Sa\xf4ne valley, the Dombes plateau, and the Beaujolais region. The whole complex reflects its triple role: a fortified military building, a seigneurial residence, and a symbol of sovereign power.","For Tr\xe9voux was no ordinary town: it became the capital of the Principality of Dombes, a former sovereign state on the border between the Kingdom of France and the Holy Roman Empire! Despite being annexed to the Kingdom of France between 1523 and 1560, the Principality of Dombes regained its political independence and kept its privileges until 1762, when it was permanently attached to France by Louis-Charles de Bourbon, who exchanged sovereignty with Louis XV.",'Just imagine: from this ch\xe2teau, the sovereign princes of Dombes minted their own currency, dispensed justice, levied taxes, and maintained their own diplomacy! A brick and stone rampart surrounded the town, with four gates built into it, turning Tr\xe9voux into a true fortified city-state. The ch\xe2teau was the heart of this city, which made Tr\xe9voux the "Monaco of its time" thanks to its trade and favorable taxation.',"The Grande Mademoiselle (Anne Marie Louise d'Orl\xe9ans), cousin of Louis XIV, made Tr\xe9voux the epicenter of a royal scandal! In 1669, she granted the principality of Dombes as an appanage to the Duke of Lauzun, whom she intended to marry. But their love angered the Sun King, who had Lauzun imprisoned at Pignerol! In 1681, under pressure from the king, he had to give up the appanages he had received in order to be freed. This story of impossible love between the wealthy heiress and the ambitious courtier filled the chronicles of Versailles and made Tr\xe9voux the setting for one of the most beautiful thwarted love stories of the Ancien R\xe9gime!","The Principality of Dombes was a true sovereign state that existed for more than three centuries, from the Bourbons in 1402 until its attachment to France in 1762! It had its own laws, its own currency, its own parliament, and even its own diplomacy. The princes of Dombes were so powerful that they could declare war, sign treaties, and receive foreign ambassadors. This near-total sovereignty was unique in France and made Tr\xe9voux a capital in its own right, rivaling \u2014 on its own scale \u2014 certain princely courts of Germany or Italy!",'The octagonal keep of the Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux is a rare architectural feat! This particular geometric shape was both aesthetic and strategic: unlike classic round towers, the octagon offered more firing angles while better withstanding bombardment. Moreover, its construction using alternating golden and white stones (a technique known as "polychrome masonry") reflects the refinement and wealth of its builders. Few French ch\xe2teaux have a keep of such a sophisticated shape, making the Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux a unique architectural gem!',"You are at the Orme panorama, offering a magnificent view from the hillside overlooking the town. The eye is naturally drawn to the Sa\xf4ne (marker A): the 9th-longest river in France, at nearly 500 km. It owes its name to the Celtic goddess Souconna (or Sauc-Onna), worshipped by the Sequani. This Celtic tribe once controlled a large part of the territories crossed by this river. When the Romans took over the area and placed this tribe under their authority, they decided to name the river accordingly.","Along the banks of the Sa\xf4ne, you can make out the towpath (marker B), which once allowed goods to be transported by barge. The relatively gentle flow of the Sa\xf4ne made this mode of transport easier. Today, the barges have been replaced by cruise boats, which can regularly be seen moored at the river stop (marker C), just steps from the campsite (marker D).","Among the town's rooftops, you can immediately spot the dome of the Montpensier Hospital (marker D), founded 350 years ago by the Duchess of Montpensier, sister of Louis XIII and cousin of King Louis XIV, when she ruled as sovereign over the whole of Dombes. The hospital was built on the town's medieval wall and thus incorporated this large round fortified tower.","Spanning the Sa\xf4ne, a footbridge (marker E) allows pedestrians and cyclists to reach Quincieux and, along the way, to cross into a new department: welcome to the Rh\xf4ne! In the middle of the footbridge, you'll be at Kilometer Point 31 (PK 31) of the Sa\xf4ne. In other words, looking to the left, there are 31 km left before the river meets the Rh\xf4ne, in Lyon. This will mark the end of its journey, which began 452 km upstream, at its source in the Vosges, at an altitude of 486m.",'\u2014 The Tree of Justice. The elm is an ornamental tree valued for its precious, very hard wood. Long used in shipbuilding for boat hulls, it is also used to make fine furniture. An interesting fact to remember: in the Middle Ages, the elm was called "the tree of justice" because it was under this tree that lords\' judges dispensed justice. It was therefore very common to find one near castles.','\u2014 River or stream? Despite its width (between 100 and 200m) and depth (up to 8m), the Sa\xf4ne is what the French call a "rivi\xe8re" rather than a "fleuve," even though in English both are simply called rivers. In French geography, a "fleuve" is a river that flows into the sea or ocean. The Sa\xf4ne is one of many rivers feeding into the Rh\xf4ne, which does flow into the Mediterranean Sea. The Sa\xf4ne joins the Rh\xf4ne at Lyon; this junction is called the confluence, which even gave its name to this "district" of Lyon.',"\u2014 The mysterious sphere. Have you noticed the strange black sphere atop the tallest mountain visible from this panorama? It's not Tintin's mysterious star, but a military radar. It is installed at the summit of Mont Verdun (626m altitude), the highest point of the Lyon Monts d'Or. It is under the control of the French Air Force base located in this area: Air Base 942 Lyon-Mont Verdun, a NATO command validation center!","You are now at the foot of the Clock Tower, a witness to the passage of time and to the municipal organization of days gone by! But before becoming a belfry, this site housed Tr\xe9voux's former arsenal. This tower was in fact built around 1405 against the arsenal buildings, which it was meant to serve as an outer defense \u2014 as shown by the cross-shaped arrow slits still visible on the lower part of the building \u2014 and it played an important role in the town's defense.","It was in 1732 that the town council voted for a loan to purchase a new clock and recast the bell \u2014 the occasion to permanently move the municipal belfry into this stone tower. Its role then became essential: the bells rang the hours, announced important events, and called the population to assemblies. In a sovereign principality like that of Dombes, having one's own belfry was no small thing: it was a declaration of autonomy carved in stone and cast in bronze.","Belfries were much more than clock towers! In the Middle Ages and the Renaissance, having one meant that the town had won its rights from its lord. These towers summoned assemblies, announced festivals and markets, and rang the alarm in times of danger. In free towns like Tr\xe9voux, the belfry was the secular equivalent of the church bell tower: a symbol of power \u2014 and independence \u2014 that some overlords would not hesitate to destroy as punishment.",'The relationship with time in the Middle Ages had nothing to do with ours! Before mechanical clocks \u2014 which appeared at the end of the 13th century \u2014 people set their schedules by church bells, which rang for religious services: matins, lauds, vespers... The municipal clock was a true revolution: it allowed "civil" time to be measured, distinct from religious time. For merchants, craftsmen, and bankers who needed precision for their business, it was an indispensable tool. Owning a public clock meant entering modernity.','Town bells had their own language. Each town developed its own codes: a certain number of strikes for a fire, another for summoning the council, another for the opening of the market... Residents immediately recognized the message \u2014 no smartphone needed! These sound "conversations" created a true municipal identity and strengthened the sense of belonging to the community. A way of communicating that our ancestors mastered without any network.','You are standing where the town fountain once stood. It was here that the town council decided in 1730 to build a public wash house, whose name gradually evolved: the "lavoir de la Font" (meaning "of the Fountain"), then the "lavoir de Lafond." The tap on the wall marks the spot where the natural water once arrived, and if you\'re curious, you can even see the original water source.','The structure you see today is not the original one: at first, the wash house was arranged the other way around and was not covered. Because it kept losing water and becoming unsanitary, it was repaired and turned around to its current layout, and covered with an overhanging roof that also protected users from the weather. Its "final" version dates to around 1875.','\u2014 Wash houses have long been misnamed. They might more accurately have been called "rinsing houses," since at first they were only used to rinse laundry, not to wash it. Washing was done at home or in farmyards. Laundry and clothes were left to soak for several days in tubs of lukewarm water mixed most often with ash (rich in potassium carbonate, a molecule with cleaning power) before being taken to the wash house to be rinsed. It was the spread of soap, which became affordable to most people by the end of the 19th century, that allowed the washing itself to move to the wash house.','\u2014 Wash houses were reserved for women: a man could even risk a fine for going there!!! In fact, the popular nicknames given to wash houses were quite sexist: "women\'s parlor," "gossip hotel," "gossip radio," or even "chatter mills." They were important gathering places in village life, where women chatted while doing their hard work, commenting on the latest news, sharing what they knew... or didn\'t know. This gave rise to the famous French word for "gossip" ("cancans"), which is a whole other story...','\u2014 Finally, it was a pandemic (the cholera outbreak of 1832\u20131834) that led to the widespread construction of wash houses across France, in order to improve general public hygiene and try to stop the spread of disease by avoiding rinsing laundry directly in waterways (springs, ponds, rivers, streams...). The arrival of the washing machine in homes (from 1950 onward) sadly marked the end of wash houses, which nevertheless remain almost "memorial" places today, as they were the quiet witnesses to the small stories and great conversations of our maternal ancestors across the centuries...',"You have almost reached the end of your adventure. First, let me congratulate you on your journey, and I invite you to take a break at the restaurant in front of you. There, you can enjoy creative cuisine made with local ingredients, a varied selection of wines, and a welcoming atmosphere.","You can also simply refresh yourself with a cold drink in the heart of Tr\xe9voux's pedestrian street. It will be the perfect way to cap off your day of exploration with a memorable culinary experience.","Here you are, in front of the Church of Saint-Symphorien, the main religious building in Tr\xe9voux. This beautiful neo-Romanesque church replaced an earlier one built in the 14th century, which had been raised to the rank of collegiate church in 1523, reflecting the religious importance of Tr\xe9voux at the time.","Having become unsuited to the town's growth, it was replaced by the current building, whose construction began in March 1899 under the direction of Lyon architects Louis Antoine Bresson, and later Tony Bourbon after the former's death in 1893. It was inaugurated in 1904, after five years of construction carried out by local craftsmen Auguste Chambon and Baptiste Faugeron.","Designed on a Latin cross plan, the church has one unusual feature: due to the lack of space on this sloped plot, it could not be oriented in the traditional way. As a result, the choir faces west and the entrance faces east \u2014 the reverse of most Catholic churches!","The sloping terrain led to considerable extra costs to stabilize the foundations, with the result that there is no bell tower \u2014 or rather, only a temporary wooden one, which is still waiting in the presbytery garden! Its position on the escarpment nonetheless gives it a majestic presence overlooking the Sa\xf4ne. The church was built on the site of the former fortress-church that once defended the Porte de Lyon, on the east side of the square where the Parliament stands.","Saint Symphorian was a young Christian martyr, born around 159 in Autun and killed around 179 during the reign of Marcus Aurelius. One day, as a statue of the goddess Cybele was being paraded through the streets of Autun to be worshipped, Symphorian refused to honor it and even mocked the procession. Arrested and questioned by the Roman governor, he declared that as a Christian he worshipped only the one true God, which led to his beheading at the age of 20. In the Merovingian era, he was regarded as a national saint, which explains the large number of churches dedicated to him across France!","The neo-Romanesque style of this church corresponds to a 19th-century architectural movement that sought to revive the grandeur of medieval Romanesque art. The most common distinctive features of neo-Romanesque buildings are barrel vaults, round-arched windows, and decorative string courses. This style was especially popular for religious buildings, as it evoked the spirituality and solidity of the great medieval abbeys, while still allowing the use of modern construction techniques.",'Early 20th-century churches often bear witness to the financial difficulties faced by towns at the time! Between construction costs, terrain constraints, and unforeseen expenses, many churches from this period had to make compromises. Some were left unfinished, others saw their bell tower projects postponed indefinitely... as is the case here in Tr\xe9voux, where the temporary wooden bell tower has been waiting in the presbytery garden for over a century! These "imperfections" are today part of the charm and authenticity of these buildings, which also tell the economic and social history of our towns.',"A few rules before you set off...","Please take care not to damage the monuments, buildings, QR codes, or any other elements essential to the app's proper functioning. Tr\xe9voux's heritage is precious; without it, discovering the town would lose all its meaning.","We recommend following the suggested routes to ensure your safety and help you discover the most beautiful spots in Tr\xe9voux. These routes have been specially chosen to give you the best possible experience.","Your safety is your own responsibility. Please stay alert to traffic and other potential hazards. The town of Tr\xe9voux accepts no liability in the event of an accident.","To fully enjoy the audio information, set your phone's volume to a level that lets you listen clearly while still appreciating the beauty of your surroundings.","For the best experience, most of the places to discover trigger automatically once you reach the spot indicated on the route. It is therefore necessary to allow location access on your device.","Please leave no litter behind and respect nature and green spaces to help preserve the beauty of Tr\xe9voux that lies before you.","Please be courteous and respectful toward the people of Tr\xe9voux. Feel free to ask them for information or advice \u2014 they'll be happy to help.","Make sure your phone is sufficiently charged before starting your visit. You may also want to bring a portable charger to avoid interruptions.","After your visit, feel free to share your feedback and suggestions with us to help improve the app and the tour routes.","You are now passing under the Villars Gate, the only remaining trace of Tr\xe9voux's former fortifications! This medieval gate, located to the northeast, is the last survivor of the four gates that once allowed entry into the fortified town. The other three \u2014 the Lyon Gate to the east, the Sa\xf4ne Gate to the south, and the Saint-Bernard Gate to the west \u2014 have unfortunately disappeared over the centuries.","Built of golden stone and brick, this gate was set into the rampart that once entirely encircled the city during the era of the Principality of Dombes. It takes its name from the Lords of Villars, who ruled the region from the 12th century onward before joining with the Lords of Thoire \u2014 forming the Thoire-Villars line, which eventually sold the fief to the Bourbons in 1402.","These fortifications were not merely symbolic: they answered a real military need. Repeated attacks from Savoy and Burgundy justified this protection. Every gate was watched, controlled, and closed at night. To pass through this gate was to enter a sovereign principality, with its own laws and its own currency! Today, it reminds us that Tr\xe9voux was far more than a simple market town: it was a true city-state at the heart of medieval Europe.","Medieval town gates were much more than simple openings in the ramparts! They served as true checkpoints where seigneurial rights were exercised. Guards checked travelers' identities, collected entry taxes, and inspected goods. Each gate kept its own hours: opening at dawn, closing at sunset. Arriving at night meant sleeping outside! These gates were often flanked by towers and equipped with portcullises, drawbridges, and arrow slits. They marked the boundary between the outside world and the protected urban space.","Building ramparts was a massive investment for medieval towns! It required mobilizing hundreds of workers for years, extracting and transporting thousands of tons of stone, and organizing forced labor among residents. In Tr\xe9voux, the rampart combined brick and stone, a technique common in the region. These fortifications weighed heavily on municipal finances for years! But it was vital: an unfortified town was at the mercy of the first passing warlord. Ramparts were therefore a guarantee of prosperity and independence.",'The names of the gates were carefully chosen and revealed the geographic organization of the time! The Lyon Gate led toward that great city, the Sa\xf4ne Gate toward the river, the Saint-Bernard Gate toward that neighboring village. This naming let travelers easily find their way: "Take the Lyon Gate if you want to reach the great southern road!" These names have survived in collective memory and still give their names to streets, squares, or neighborhoods today. They tell the story of trade and relations between territories in medieval times.',"Leave the tour?","Your progress on this route won't be saved. You'll need to start this step over if you come back later.","Leave the tour","Continue the tour","You're not at the starting point","You seem far from this stage's starting point. Would you like directions to get there?","Take me there","Continue without directions","Go to start","Couldn't calculate the route right now.","On foot","By car","By bike","This feature is currently under development. Come back soon to discover it!","OK","Recenter","Well done, you've completed the tour!","You've explored the historic heart of Tr\xe9voux and discovered its rich heritage. Thank you for taking this tour!","{distance} walked","I just finished the Tr\xe9voux tour! \ud83c\udff0\ud83d\udeb6","Share","See my travel journal","To explore","Your souvenir photos","Rewards","Your earned badges","See my rewards","Back to home","N","Location required","This feature needs your position to guide you and detect your arrival. Please allow location access to continue.","Location access was denied. Open the app settings to enable it, then come back here.","Location (GPS) is turned off on your phone. Turn it on in settings to continue.","Allow location","Open app settings","Turn on location","Not now",'Choosing "Not now" will end the current tour: location is required to continue.',"Update required","A new version of the app is available and must be installed to continue.","Update now","Legal information","Legal notice","Terms of use","Privacy","The reference version of this policy is available online:","View online","Close","Legal information","S","W","E","\ud83c\udf33 The Wise Oak","Welcome, young apprentice knight! Legend has it that an ancient oak once stood here, witness to the birth of Tr\xe9voux Castle. No one knows if this tale is true, but the elders used to say its roots kept the secrets of our history.","How many main branches does this majestic oak have?","Between 3 and 4 branches","Between 5 and 7 branches","Between 8 and 10 branches","More than 10 branches","Look carefully towards the top of the tree, and only count the largest branches coming from the main trunk.","\ud83d\udc41\ufe0f The Watchman's Stone","Legend has it that an old stone once served as a lookout post here for the guards of Tr\xe9voux Castle, who watched over the Sa\xf4ne river and the roads leading to the fortress. Like many knights of the time, they used their own codes and symbols to recognize one another.","What did knights mainly engrave on their shields to stand out in battle?","Crossed swords","Their family coats of arms","Castle towers","Royal fleur-de-lis","Each noble family had its own hereditary colors and symbols to be recognized.","\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f The Tree of Coats of Arms","It's said that an old tree in this forest once bore coats of arms carved into its bark, in memory of the lords of Tr\xe9voux. Like all nobles, they had their own heraldry, adorning shields, banners, and castle walls.","What were the most noble traditional colors used in medieval coats of arms?","Red and gold (yellow gold)","Blue and silver (white)","Green and purple","Black and white only","Precious metals (gold and silver) were considered the noblest colors in heraldry.","\ud83c\udf3f The Herbalists' Grove","According to legend, the castle's monks once came here to grow a garden of medicinal herbs, so precious in the Middle Ages. Their knowledge of botany was said to be immense, healing the people of Tr\xe9voux with natural remedies.","Which plant was particularly renowned in the Middle Ages for treating headaches and improving memory?","Fresh mint","Wild thyme","Common sage","All of these plants","The monks knew well the virtues of many aromatic plants from our regions.","\ud83d\udc8e The Treasure Clearing","Congratulations, brave knight! You've just crossed the secret clearing of the forest guardians of Tr\xe9voux \u2014 or so the legend goes. Your journey ends here, but remember that the real adventure only begins when you set out to discover our heritage.","According to the wisdom of ancient knights, what is the greatest treasure a hero can discover?","A chest full of gold","A magic sword","Knowledge and wisdom","A scroll of secrets","True heroes know that the most precious wealth cannot be measured in gold coins.","Badge of the Sage","Badge of the Watchman","Badge of the Coats of Arms","Badge of the Herbalist","Badge of the Treasure","The Forest Map","See my treasure","The Oak of Secrets","Memory game","Beneath its old roots, the Oak hides pairs of secrets. Find them all to earn its trust!","The Watcher's Stone","Forest riddles","The Watcher has guarded the forest since the beginning of time. Answer its riddles to prove your wisdom.","I blow without ever being seen, I make the leaves dance and the seeds travel. What am I?","Rain","Wind","Sun","River","I carry my house on my back and leave a shiny trail behind me. What am I?","Hedgehog","Slug","Snail","Lizard","The older I get, the taller I grow. My arms touch the sky and my feet drink the earth. What am I?","Tree","River","Mountain","Cloud","The Tree of Crests","Rhythm game","Watch the forest guardians pass by carefully, then replay their round in the right order.","The Herbalists' Grove","Sorting game","A mischievous goblin mixed up his treasure with his pranks! Help the Herbalist sort the real from the fake.","Real treasure","Goblin prank","A wild strawberry","A blueberry","A chestnut","A prankster's mask","A rigged deck of cards","A glass ball","The Treasure Clearing","Final challenge","The chest has shattered into pieces! Tap two pieces to swap them and rebuild the treasure's picture.","Leave the quest?","Your progress is already saved, but this mini-game will restart if you come back.","Leave","Keep playing","Continue","Badge earned!","Not quite... try again!","{count} moves","Watch closely...","Your turn!","The Forest Quest","Welcome, young adventurer! I am the guardian of this enchanted forest. Explore my 5 clearings, solve their challenges, and discover the treasure hidden at the end of the path!","Start the adventure","Tap the first clearing to get started!","On to the next clearing!","Well done, adventurer! Every clearing is explored \u2014 go claim your treasure!","You're halfway there, keep it up!","Well done! Next round!","Almost there, last round!","Skip this activity","Welcome to the forest of Tr\xe9voux! Old legends are told here, passed down from generation to generation. No one knows what's true, but they deserve to be told. Discover them, chapter by chapter.","Start the quest","Time remaining: "," steps","Ready to discover the next part of the legend?","Discover this chapter","Reset the quest","Need a hint?","Well done! Correct answer!","Try again! Use the hint if needed.","A new chapter awaits you!","French content","The forest quest is only available in French for now (text and audio). You can still access it, or skip this step.","Access anyway","Skip","The Enchanted Forest","Leave the visit?","Are you sure you want to leave the visit?","Cancel","Leave","Skip the quest","Skip the forest quest?","You can always come back to it another time. Skip anyway?","Yes, skip","No, continue the quest","Congratulations, Knight!","You have brilliantly completed the Quest of the Guardians of the Tr\xe9voux Forest! Your courage and wisdom have led you to victory.","Time's up!","The time allotted for your quest has run out, but don't be discouraged! Every adventure is a chance to learn. You can start again to improve your score!"," steps completed out of "," badges earned","No badges collected this time.\nTry again for another chance!","Restart the quest","Continue the visit","Share my diploma","I took on the challenge of the Tr\xe9voux Forest Guardians' Quest! \ud83c\udfc6\ud83c\udf33","Your opinion matters to us!","You've just finished your visit. A review on the store helps us a lot to improve the app and to help others discover it.","Rate the app","Later","Coming soon!","This feature is currently in development. Check back soon to discover it!","OK","Coming\nsoon","Our Places","Our Places","Tours","List","Map","See full details","Destination reached!","You have arrived at {place}. Ready to discover this place?","Discover this place","Take me there","Navigating\u2026","Rate this place","I recommend it","Not for me","Add a comment? (optional)","Send","Thanks for your feedback!","Your comment will be visible after a quick review.","Close","Couldn't send your review right now.","This comment can't be sent as-is.","Report a problem","Report a problem","What's the problem?","QR code unreadable or broken","GPS isn't triggering","Problem with the audio guide","Error in a text or photo","Other","Describe the problem (optional)","Send report","Report sent","Thank you, we'll look into it quickly.","Failed to send. Check your connection and try again.","Retry","Close","Reviews","{percent}% of visitors recommend it","Be the first to share your opinion!","This place already has reviews!","Rate this place","You've already reviewed this place","Discover the emblematic Ch\xe2teau de Tr\xe9voux, a witness to the history of the Dombes region and former seat of parliament.","Visit this beautiful Gothic church and discover its rich artistic and spiritual heritage.","Admire this historic tower overlooking the town, standing proudly at the heart of the city.","Enjoy an exceptional panorama over the Sa\xf4ne valley and the Beaujolais hills.","Pass through this medieval gate, a remnant of the town's ancient fortifications.","Dive into local heritage with this beautifully restored 19th-century wash house.","Enjoy a stop at this magnificent parliament of the Dombes and its superb frescoes.","Discover this emblematic street of Tr\xe9voux and its art workshops.","Audio guide","Audio guide available","Audio guide not available in your language","Have you arrived?","Checking your location","You still seem to be {distance} from the location. Get closer, or confirm if you've really arrived.","We can't check your location right now (no GPS signal). You can try again, or continue if you've really arrived.","Continue anyway","Try again","Want the full experience?","Download the Tr\xe9voux app to follow the whole tour, unlock the challenges and more.","Download for Android","Download for iPhone","About","Photo gallery","Scan a QR code","Scan","Scan a place's QR code to access it directly","QR Code not recognized","Scan cancelled","Next stop","Stage duration: ","Total remaining time: "," min","Continue","The Enchanted Forest","End of the tour","Resume your visit?","You have a tour in progress. Would you like to pick up where you left off, or start over?","Resume","Start over","You're in Tr\xe9voux!","Make the most of it and discover the town with our guided tour.","Discover now","Later","Travel journal","My travel journal","A souvenir photo for each place you visit \u2014 tap the camera icon to add one.","Forest badges","Take a photo","Choose from gallery","Delete this photo?","This souvenir photo will be permanently removed from the travel journal.","Delete","Cancel","Share my certificate","My Tr\xe9voux travel journal","A keepsake of your time in town","Share my journal","Download","Your Tr\xe9voux souvenir","Travel journal","Tr\xe9voux","Explored with Flan\xe9a, the app that brings Tr\xe9voux to life.","Image saved to your gallery!","Couldn't save the image.","Generating image...","Capture the moment!","Take a souvenir photo of this place: it stays in the app, added to your personal travel journal. You can view it anytime, and download the full journal at the end of the tour.","Take a photo","Later","Highlight","How many basins do you see in the wash house?","Look closely inside, they sit side by side.","Well spotted!","How many floors does the clock tower have?","Look up and count the levels, from bottom to top.","Exactly right, great eye!","True or false: an oak tree can live for more than 100 years.","Think about the size and age of the biggest trees you know.","Well done, little naturalist!","What shape is the gate's opening?","Round, arched","Square","Triangular","Look at the top of the opening \u2014 is it straight or curved?","Great spot!","How many towers do you see on the castle?","Look all around without moving your feet.","Great, you found them all!","What do you see on the horizon from this viewpoint?","Look far away, beyond the rooftops.","Wonderful, you have a great eye!","What symbol do you see on the church's fa\xe7ade?","A cross","A star","A coat of arms","Look right at the top, in the middle of the fa\xe7ade.","Well spotted, champion!","Create your hero!","What's your name?","Your first name","Choose your avatar","Knight","Princess","Explorer","Wizard","Hi {name}!","puzzle pieces","Continue the adventure","Well done, you've finished every step!","Locked","In progress","Done","Need a hint?","Skip","Skip this challenge?","You can always try again another time. Skip anyway?","Yes, skip","No, I'll try again","Almost! Try again \ud83d\udcaa","True","False","Confirm","New puzzle piece!","Take the challenge!","Almost there, keep going!","Congratulations, {name}!","You've completed the Tr\xe9voux Adventure Trail brilliantly!","Adventurer's Diploma","certifies that {name} explored the secrets of Tr\xe9voux and completed every challenge of the Adventure Trail.","I finished the Tr\xe9voux Adventure Trail with {name}! \ud83c\udfc6\ud83e\udde9","Share","Scratch the screen with your finger to reveal your puzzle!","Reveal everything","Back to home","Spin the reward wheel","Reward wheel coming soon","Adventure Trail","Duration","Recommended age","Fitness level","Who's it for?","Cancel","Here's the route","A travel journal, just for you","During the visit, the app will suggest taking a photo at each place. It stays in the app, added to your personal travel journal: viewable anytime, and downloadable at the end of the tour.","This route is not stroller-accessible.","About 1h30 to 2h","Ages 12 and up recommended",u.o,"Everyone welcome","Discover the hidden treasures of Tr\xe9voux on a guided stroll: castle, clock tower, wash house and more, at your own pace.","About 1h30 to 2h","Ages 6 and up",u.o,"Families, with kids","Experience the cultural route in game mode! Your hero takes on a challenge at each spot, collects puzzle pieces, and earns a diploma at the end of the adventure."],t.l)
B.Lj=new A.bp(B.eP,["trevouxapp","Inicio","Escanear QR","Nuestros lugares","Continuar","\xa1Vamos all\xe1!","Iniciar la visita guiada","Continuar","\xbfEst\xe1s listo?","La aventura comienza en...","Recorrido cultural","Caza en el bosque","Trofeos","Mi progreso","Tus lugares visitados y tus trofeos de recorrido","Lugares visitados"," lugares visitados de ","Recorridos y trofeos","Bloqueado","\xa1Desbloqueado!","Probar mi suerte","Ver mi premio","Pr\xf3ximamente","\xa1Gira la ruleta!","Girar la ruleta","\xa1Enhorabuena!","Tu c\xf3digo","Muestra este c\xf3digo a un comercio asociado para disfrutar tu premio.","Premio ya obtenido","-10% en un restaurante asociado","Una bebida gratis","Un postre gratis","-5% en un comercio asociado","Un recuerdo sorpresa","Vuelve a intentarlo otra vez","De acuerdo","Solo un giro por dispositivo y por d\xeda. \xa1Int\xe9ntalo ma\xf1ana!","La ruleta de premios no est\xe1 disponible en este momento.","No se pudo girar la ruleta. Comprueba tu conexi\xf3n e int\xe9ntalo de nuevo.","\xbfLo sab\xedas?","Descubra el castillo de Tr\xe9voux","Un paseo junto al r\xedo Saona","El mercado del s\xe1bado por la ma\xf1ana","Estimados viajeros, \xa1bienvenidos a Tr\xe9voux! Descubrir\xe1n los secretos y la historia de esta maravillosa ciudad medieval.","\xa1Vamos all\xe1!","Antes de comenzar su recorrido, seleccione su itinerario.","Recorrido cultural","Recorrido l\xfadico","Una \xfaltima cosa.. \xbfCu\xe1l es su medio de transporte?","Voy en bicicleta","Voy en coche","Voy a pie","\ud83c\udff0 La b\xfasqueda de los Guardianes\ndel Bosque de Tr\xe9voux","\u23f1\ufe0f Tiempo restante: 15:00","\ud83d\udcc8 Tu progreso","0/5","\ud83c\udfc5 Colecci\xf3n de insignias","\ud83d\ude80 Comenzar la Aventura","\ud83d\udcf1 Escanear el C\xf3digo QR","\ud83d\udd04 Intentar de nuevo","T\xedtulo de la etapa","Descripci\xf3n de la etapa","\ud83c\udfa7 Escuchar la historia","\ud83d\udca1 ayuda","\ud83d\udca1 La pista aparece aqu\xed","\xa1Descubre la historia de Tr\xe9voux a trav\xe9s de esta aventura interactiva! \ud83c\udf1f","Castillo de Tr\xe9voux","Panorama de l'Orme","Rue des Arts","El antiguo parlamento del Dombes","El lavadero de Tr\xe9voux","La Torre del Reloj","La Iglesia","La Puerta de Villars","Ir a visitar","Vista previa de im\xe1genes","El Castillo","Descubra el emblem\xe1tico castillo de Tr\xe9voux, testigo de la historia del Dombes y antigua sede de su parlamento.","\ud83e\udded Iniciar la navegaci\xf3n","Castillo de Tr\xe9voux","Castillo de Tr\xe9voux","Castillo de Tr\xe9voux","Escanea y Descubre","\ud83c\udfc6 \xa1Felicidades, Caballero!","Mensaje de felicitaci\xf3n","\ud83d\udcca Tus Estad\xedsticas","Estad\xedsticas de la misi\xf3n","\ud83d\udcdc Tu Certificado","\ud83d\udcbe Descargar el Certificado","\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Insignias Obtenidas","\ud83d\udcf1 Compartir mis Resultados","\ud83d\udd04 Reiniciar la Misi\xf3n","Continuar la visita","\xa1Gracias por participar en esta aventura en el bosque de Tr\xe9voux!","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","Pr\xf3xima etapa","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: 10 minutos","Duraci\xf3n total restante: 30 minutos","Continuar","El Castillo","Estimados viajeros, est\xe1n a punto de adentrarse en el coraz\xf3n de la historia de Tr\xe9voux descubriendo su castillo medieval. Dominando la ciudad y el r\xedo Saona, este edificio emblem\xe1tico es testigo del prestigioso pasado de la antigua capital del Principado de Dombes.","Antes de llegar a sus murallas, d\xe9jense encantar por un agradable paseo por las pintorescas callejuelas del casco antiguo. Una vez all\xed, disfruten de un panorama excepcional y sum\xe9rjanse en los relatos fascinantes de este lugar cargado de historia. \xa1Prep\xe1rense para un viaje en el tiempo en el que cada piedra cuenta una historia!","Iniciar la navegaci\xf3n","Navegaci\xf3n2","Abrir el men\xfa de navegaci\xf3n","Cerrar el men\xfa de navegaci\xf3n","Android Studio","android.studio@android.com","Encabezado de navegaci\xf3n","Ajustes","Inicio","Galer\xeda","Presentaci\xf3n","MapsActivity","Se encuentran ahora frente al castillo de Tr\xe9voux, \xa1s\xedmbolo de poder y testigo de cinco siglos de extraordinaria historia! Esta fortaleza fue construida hacia 1300 por los se\xf1ores de Thoire-Villars para vigilar el puerto y el peaje sobre el r\xedo Saona. Pero es en 1402 cuando todo cambia: el \xfaltimo de los Thoire-Villars vende el feudo a Luis II de Borb\xf3n, dando origen a uno de los principados m\xe1s fascinantes de Europa.","Construido en dos fases principales durante el siglo XIV, este castillo fortificado de piedra es un edificio imponente, clasificado como Monumento Hist\xf3rico desde 1913. Su exclusiva torre del homenaje octogonal, decorada con piedras doradas y blancas, alcanzaba antiguamente los 28 metros de altura \u2014hoy reducida a 16 metros tras la Revoluci\xf3n\u2014 y a\xfan ofrece un panorama excepcional sobre el valle del r\xedo Saona, la meseta del Dombes y el Beaujolais. El conjunto refleja su triple funci\xf3n: edificio militar fortificado, residencia se\xf1orial y s\xedmbolo de poder soberano.","Porque Tr\xe9voux no fue una ciudad cualquiera: se convirti\xf3 en la capital del Principado de Dombes, un antiguo estado soberano en la frontera entre el reino de Francia y el Sacro Imperio Romano Germ\xe1nico. A pesar de ser anexionado al reino de Francia entre 1523 y 1560, el Principado de Dombes recuper\xf3 su independencia pol\xedtica y conserv\xf3 sus privilegios hasta 1762, fecha de su definitiva incorporaci\xf3n a Francia por Louis-Charles de Bourbon, quien intercambi\xf3 la soberan\xeda con Luis XV.",'Imaginen: desde este castillo, los pr\xedncipes soberanos de Dombes acu\xf1aban su propia moneda, impart\xedan justicia, recaudaban impuestos y manten\xedan su propia diplomacia. En aquella \xe9poca, una muralla de ladrillo y piedra rodeaba la ciudad, con cuatro puertas construidas en ella, convirtiendo a Tr\xe9voux en una aut\xe9ntica ciudad-estado fortificada. El castillo era el coraz\xf3n de esta ciudad, que gracias a su comercio y a su fiscalidad ventajosa se convirti\xf3 en el "M\xf3naco de la \xe9poca".',"La Grande Mademoiselle (Ana Mar\xeda Luisa de Orleans), prima de Luis XIV, convirti\xf3 a Tr\xe9voux en el epicentro de un esc\xe1ndalo real. En 1669 concedi\xf3, como apanaje, el principado de Dombes al duque de Lauzun, con quien pretend\xeda casarse. Pero ese amor contrari\xf3 al Rey Sol, \xa1que hizo encarcelar a Lauzun en Pignerol! En 1681, bajo la presi\xf3n del rey, tuvo que renunciar a los apanajes recibidos para ser liberado. Esta historia de amor imposible entre la riqu\xedsima heredera y el ambicioso cortesano aliment\xf3 las cr\xf3nicas de Versalles e hizo de Tr\xe9voux el escenario de una de las m\xe1s bellas historias de amor contrariado del Antiguo R\xe9gimen.","\xa1El Principado de Dombes fue un verdadero estado soberano que existi\xf3 durante m\xe1s de tres siglos, desde los Borb\xf3n en 1402 hasta su anexi\xf3n a Francia en 1762! Ten\xeda sus propias leyes, su propia moneda, su propio parlamento e incluso su propia diplomacia. Los pr\xedncipes de Dombes eran tan poderosos que pod\xedan declarar la guerra, firmar tratados y recibir embajadores extranjeros. Esta soberan\xeda casi total era \xfanica en Francia y convert\xeda a Tr\xe9voux en una aut\xe9ntica capital, capaz de rivalizar, a su escala, con algunas cortes principescas de Alemania o Italia.",'\xa1La torre del homenaje octogonal del castillo de Tr\xe9voux es una rara proeza arquitect\xf3nica! Esta particular forma geom\xe9trica era a la vez est\xe9tica y estrat\xe9gica: a diferencia de las torres redondas cl\xe1sicas, el oct\xf3gono ofrec\xeda m\xe1s \xe1ngulos de tiro a la vez que resist\xeda mejor los bombardeos. Adem\xe1s, su construcci\xf3n con piedras doradas y blancas alternadas (t\xe9cnica llamada "aparejo policromo") refleja el refinamiento y la riqueza de sus constructores. Pocos castillos franceses poseen una torre del homenaje de una forma tan sofisticada, lo que hace del castillo de Tr\xe9voux una joya arquitect\xf3nica \xfanica.',"Se encuentran en el mirador de l'Orme, que ofrece una vista magn\xedfica desde la ladera de la colina y en posici\xf3n elevada sobre la ciudad. La mirada se dirige naturalmente hacia el r\xedo Saona (punto A): el 9\xba r\xedo m\xe1s largo de Francia, con casi 500 km. Debe su nombre a la diosa celta Souconna (o Sauc-Onna), venerada por los secuanos. Esta tribu celta controlaba en su d\xeda gran parte de los territorios atravesados por este curso de agua. Los romanos, al tomar posesi\xf3n del lugar y someter a esta tribu a su autoridad, decidieron entonces dar este nombre al r\xedo.","A orillas del r\xedo Saona se distingue el camino de sirga (punto B), que antiguamente permit\xeda transportar mercanc\xedas en gabarras. El caudal relativamente tranquilo del Saona facilitaba este modo de transporte. Hoy en d\xeda, las gabarras han dado paso a los barcos de crucero, que pueden verse regularmente amarrados en el embarcadero fluvial (punto C), a dos pasos del c\xe1mping (punto D).","Entre los tejados de la ciudad, se distingue de inmediato la c\xfapula del hospital Montpensier (punto D), fundado hace 350 a\xf1os por la duquesa de Montpensier, hermana de Luis XIII y prima del rey Luis XIV, cuando ella reinaba como soberana sobre todo el Dombes. El hospital fue edificado sobre la muralla medieval de la ciudad e incorpor\xf3 as\xed esta gran torre redonda de fortificaci\xf3n.","Cruzando el r\xedo Saona, una pasarela (punto E) permite a peatones y ciclistas llegar a Quincieux y, de paso, cambiar de departamento: \xa1bienvenidos al R\xf3dano! En medio de la pasarela se encontrar\xe1n en el Punto Kilom\xe9trico 31 (PK 31) del Saona. Es decir, mirando hacia la izquierda, quedan 31 km antes de la confluencia del r\xedo con el R\xf3dano, en Lyon. Ese ser\xe1 el final de su recorrido, iniciado 452 km r\xedo arriba, en su nacimiento, en los Vosgos, a 486 m de altitud.",'\u2013 El \xe1rbol de la justicia. El olmo es un \xe1rbol ornamental noble, de madera preciosa y muy dura. Utilizado durante mucho tiempo en la marina para los cascos de los barcos, tambi\xe9n sirve para la fabricaci\xf3n de muebles refinados. Una an\xe9cdota interesante que recordar: en la Edad Media, el olmo era llamado "el \xe1rbol de la justicia", porque era bajo este \xe1rbol donde los jueces de los se\xf1ores impart\xedan justicia. Era, por tanto, muy frecuente encontrarlos cerca de los castillos.','\u2013 \xbfR\xedo grande o r\xedo peque\xf1o? A pesar de su anchura (entre 100 y 200 m) y su profundidad (hasta 8 m), el Saona es, seg\xfan la clasificaci\xf3n tradicional francesa, un "r\xedo" que desemboca en otro r\xedo, y no un curso de agua que desemboca directamente en el mar, como podr\xeda pensarse. En franc\xe9s, un "fleuve" es un curso de agua que termina en el mar o el oc\xe9ano. El Saona forma as\xed parte de los numerosos r\xedos que alimentan al R\xf3dano, el cual s\xed desemboca en el mar Mediterr\xe1neo. El Saona se une al R\xf3dano en Lyon; a este punto de encuentro se le llama confluencia, lo que adem\xe1s dio nombre a este "barrio" de Lyon.',"\u2013 La misteriosa esfera. \xbfHan notado la extra\xf1a esfera negra en la cima de la monta\xf1a m\xe1s alta visible desde este mirador? No se trata de la misteriosa estrella de Tint\xedn, sino de un radar militar. Est\xe1 instalado en la cima del Mont Verdun (626 m de altitud), el punto m\xe1s alto de los Monts d'Or de Lyon. Est\xe1 bajo el control de la base a\xe9rea del ej\xe9rcito franc\xe9s instalada en esta zona: la base a\xe9rea 942 Lyon-Mont Verdun, \xa1centro de validaci\xf3n de mando de la OTAN!","Se encuentran aqu\xed, al pie de la torre del reloj, testigo del paso del tiempo y de la organizaci\xf3n municipal de anta\xf1o. Pero antes de ser un campanario, este emplazamiento albergaba el antiguo arsenal de Tr\xe9voux. Esta torre fue, en efecto, construida hacia 1405 junto a los edificios del arsenal, al que deb\xeda servir de avanzada, como a\xfan atestiguan las aspilleras cruciformes visibles en la parte baja del edificio, y desempe\xf1aba un papel importante en la defensa de la ciudad.","Fue en 1732 cuando el consejo de la ciudad aprob\xf3 un pr\xe9stamo para la compra de un nuevo reloj y la refundici\xf3n de la campana, ocasi\xf3n que se aprovech\xf3 para trasladar definitivamente el campanario municipal a esta torre de piedra. Su papel se volvi\xf3 entonces esencial: las campanas marcaban las horas, anunciaban los acontecimientos importantes y convocaban a la poblaci\xf3n a las asambleas. En un principado soberano como el de Dombes, tener un campanario propio no era poca cosa: era una declaraci\xf3n de autonom\xeda tallada en piedra y fundida en bronce.","\xa1Los campanarios eran mucho m\xe1s que simples torres con reloj! En la Edad Media y el Renacimiento, tener uno significaba que la ciudad hab\xeda arrancado sus derechos a su se\xf1or. Estas torres convocaban las asambleas, anunciaban las fiestas y los mercados, tocaban la alarma en caso de peligro. En las ciudades libres como Tr\xe9voux, el campanario era el equivalente laico del campanario de la iglesia: un s\xedmbolo de poder \u2014e independencia\u2014 que algunos se\xf1ores feudales no dudaban en hacer destruir a modo de castigo.",'\xa1La relaci\xf3n con el tiempo en la Edad Media no ten\xeda nada que ver con la nuestra! Antes de los relojes mec\xe1nicos \u2014que aparecieron a finales del siglo XIII\u2014 la gente se guiaba por las campanas de las iglesias, que marcaban los oficios religiosos: maitines, laudes, v\xedsperas... El reloj municipal supuso una verdadera revoluci\xf3n: permit\xeda medir un tiempo "civil", distinto del tiempo religioso. Para comerciantes, artesanos y banqueros, que necesitaban precisi\xf3n para sus negocios, era una herramienta indispensable. Tener un reloj p\xfablico significaba entrar en la modernidad.','Las campanas comunales ten\xedan su propio lenguaje. Cada ciudad desarrollaba sus propios c\xf3digos: tantos toques para un incendio, tantos para convocar al consejo, tantos para la apertura del mercado... Los habitantes reconoc\xedan de inmediato el mensaje \u2014\xa1sin necesidad de smartphone! Estas "conversaciones" sonoras creaban una verdadera identidad municipal y reforzaban el sentimiento de pertenencia a la comunidad. Un arte de comunicar que nuestros antepasados dominaban sin ninguna red.',"Se encuentran en el lugar donde antiguamente se hallaba la fuente de la ciudad. Fue aqu\xed donde el consejo municipal decidi\xf3, en 1730, construir un lavadero p\xfablico cuyo nombre fue evolucionando poco a poco: lavadero de la Fuente, y m\xe1s tarde lavadero de Lafond. El grifo en la pared permite ver el punto por donde antiguamente llegaba el agua natural, y si sienten curiosidad, incluso pueden observar la fuente de agua original.",'La construcci\xf3n que ven hoy no es la original: al principio, el lavadero estaba dispuesto al rev\xe9s y no estaba cubierto. Debido a que perd\xeda agua y se volv\xeda insalubre, fue reparado y transformado para colocarlo en su orientaci\xf3n actual y cubrirlo con un tejado saliente, que tambi\xe9n proteg\xeda a las usuarias de las inclemencias del tiempo. Su versi\xf3n "definitiva" se fechar\xeda as\xed hacia 1875.','\u2013 Los lavaderos llevaron durante mucho tiempo un nombre enga\xf1oso. Podr\xedan haberse llamado "enjuagaderos", pues al principio solo serv\xedan para enjuagar la ropa, no para lavarla. El lavado propiamente dicho se hac\xeda en casa o en el patio de las granjas. La ropa se dejaba en remojo varios d\xedas en cubas de agua tibia mezclada la mayor\xeda de las veces con ceniza (rica en carbonato de potasio, mol\xe9cula con poder limpiador), antes de llevarla al lavadero para enjuagarla. Fue la generalizaci\xf3n del jab\xf3n, que se hizo asequible para la mayor\xeda de la poblaci\xf3n a finales del siglo XIX, lo que permiti\xf3 "trasladar" la operaci\xf3n de lavado propiamente dicha al lavadero.','\u2013 \xa1Los lavaderos estaban reservados a las mujeres: un hombre pod\xeda incluso arriesgarse a una multa por acudir all\xed! Por lo dem\xe1s, los apodos populares dados a los lavaderos eran bastante sexistas: "parlamento de las mujeres", "hotel del cotilleo", "radio-lavaderos" o incluso "molinos de palabras". Eran lugares importantes de la vida del pueblo, donde las mujeres charlaban durante su duro trabajo, comentando las \xfaltimas noticias, contando lo que sab\xedan... o lo que no sab\xedan. De ah\xed surgi\xf3 la famosa expresi\xf3n francesa "cancans" para referirse a los chismes, aunque esa es otra historia...','\u2013 Por \xfaltimo, fue una pandemia (la del c\xf3lera de 1832\u20131834) la que llev\xf3 a construir masivamente lavaderos por toda Francia, con el fin de mejorar la higiene general de la poblaci\xf3n e intentar frenar la transmisi\xf3n de enfermedades evitando enjuagar la ropa directamente en los cursos de agua (manantiales, charcas, r\xedos...). La llegada de la lavadora a los hogares (a partir de 1950) marc\xf3, lamentablemente, el fin de los lavaderos, que sin embargo siguen siendo hoy lugares casi "de memoria", pues fueron testigos silenciosos de peque\xf1as historias y grandes conversaciones de nuestras antepasadas maternas a lo largo de varios siglos...',"Est\xe1n a punto de llegar al final de su aventura. Antes de nada, quiero felicitarles por su recorrido, y les propongo hacer una parada en el restaurante que tienen frente a ustedes. En este restaurante podr\xe1n disfrutar de una cocina creativa con ingredientes locales, una variada selecci\xf3n de vinos y un ambiente acogedor.","Tambi\xe9n podr\xe1n simplemente refrescarse con una bebida fr\xeda en pleno coraz\xf3n de la calle peatonal de Tr\xe9voux. Culminar\xe1n as\xed su jornada de exploraci\xf3n con una experiencia culinaria memorable.","Aqu\xed tienen, frente a la iglesia de Saint-Symphorien, el principal edificio religioso de Tr\xe9voux. Esta bella iglesia de estilo neorrom\xe1nico sustituy\xf3 a una primera iglesia construida en el siglo XIV, que hab\xeda sido elevada al rango de colegiata en 1523, lo que refleja la importancia religiosa de Tr\xe9voux en aquella \xe9poca.","Al quedar inadecuada para la expansi\xf3n de la ciudad, fue sustituida por el edificio actual, cuyas obras comenzaron en marzo de 1899 bajo la direcci\xf3n de los arquitectos lioneses Louis Antoine Bresson y, tras su fallecimiento en 1893, Tony Bourbon. Fue inaugurada en 1904, tras cinco a\xf1os de construcci\xf3n llevada a cabo por los artesanos locales Auguste Chambon y Baptiste Faugeron.","Concebida seg\xfan una planta de cruz latina, la iglesia presenta una particularidad: por falta de espacio en este terreno en pendiente, no pudo orientarse seg\xfan la tradici\xf3n. As\xed, el coro mira hacia el oeste y la entrada hacia el este, \xa1lo contrario de la gran mayor\xeda de las iglesias cat\xf3licas!","La configuraci\xf3n del terreno en pendiente ocasion\xf3 unos sobrecostes considerables para estabilizar los cimientos, con el resultado de que no hay campanario, o mejor dicho, solo un campanario provisional de madera que sigue esperando en el jard\xedn de la casa parroquial. Su posici\xf3n sobre el escarpe le confiere, sin embargo, un aspecto majestuoso que domina el r\xedo Saona. La iglesia fue edificada en el emplazamiento de la antigua iglesia-fortaleza que en su d\xeda defend\xeda la Puerta de Lyon, en el lado este de la plaza donde se encuentra el Parlamento.","San Sinforiano fue un joven m\xe1rtir cristiano, nacido hacia el a\xf1o 159 en Autun y muerto hacia el 179 bajo el reinado de Marco Aurelio. Un d\xeda, mientras la estatua de la diosa Cibeles era paseada por las calles de Autun para ser venerada, Sinforiano se neg\xf3 a honrarla e incluso se burl\xf3 del cortejo. Detenido e interrogado por el gobernador romano, afirm\xf3 que, como cristiano, solo adoraba al \xfanico Dios verdadero, lo que le vali\xf3 ser decapitado a los 20 a\xf1os. En la \xe9poca merovingia era considerado un santo nacional, de ah\xed el gran n\xfamero de iglesias que le est\xe1n dedicadas en Francia.","El estilo neorrom\xe1nico de esta iglesia corresponde a un movimiento arquitect\xf3nico del siglo XIX que buscaba recuperar la grandeza del arte rom\xe1nico medieval. Las caracter\xedsticas distintivas m\xe1s habituales de los edificios neorrom\xe1nicos son las b\xf3vedas de ca\xf1\xf3n, las ventanas de arco de medio punto y las cornisas. Este estilo era especialmente apreciado para los edificios religiosos, ya que evocaba la espiritualidad y la solidez de las grandes abad\xedas de la Edad Media, al tiempo que permit\xeda el uso de t\xe9cnicas de construcci\xf3n modernas.",'\xa1Las iglesias de principios del siglo XX suelen dar testimonio de las dificultades financieras de los municipios de la \xe9poca! Entre los costes de construcci\xf3n, las limitaciones del terreno y los imprevistos, muchas iglesias de este per\xedodo tuvieron que hacer concesiones. Algunas quedaron inacabadas, otras vieron sus proyectos de campanario aplazados indefinidamente... como aqu\xed en Tr\xe9voux, donde el campanario provisional de madera sigue esperando en el jard\xedn de la casa parroquial desde hace m\xe1s de un siglo. Estas "imperfecciones" son hoy en d\xeda todo el encanto y la autenticidad de estos edificios, que tambi\xe9n narran la historia econ\xf3mica y social de nuestras ciudades.',"Algunas normas antes de partir...","Procuren no da\xf1ar los monumentos, los edificios, los c\xf3digos QR ni ning\xfan otro elemento esencial para el buen funcionamiento de la aplicaci\xf3n. El patrimonio de Tr\xe9voux es un tesoro; sin \xe9l, descubrir la ciudad perder\xeda todo su sentido.","Les recomendamos seguir los itinerarios propuestos para garantizar su seguridad y permitirles descubrir los lugares m\xe1s bonitos de Tr\xe9voux. Estos recorridos han sido especialmente dise\xf1ados para ofrecerles la mejor experiencia posible.","Su seguridad es responsabilidad suya. Est\xe9n atentos al tr\xe1fico y a otros posibles peligros. El ayuntamiento de Tr\xe9voux declina toda responsabilidad en caso de accidente.","Para disfrutar plenamente de la informaci\xf3n en audio, ajusten el volumen de su tel\xe9fono a un nivel que les permita escuchar bien sin dejar de disfrutar de la belleza del entorno.","Para una experiencia \xf3ptima, la mayor\xeda de los lugares por descubrir se activan autom\xe1ticamente al llegar al punto indicado en el itinerario. Por ello, es necesario autorizar el acceso a la ubicaci\xf3n de su dispositivo.","No dejen ning\xfan residuo tras de s\xed y respeten la naturaleza y los espacios verdes para preservar la belleza de Tr\xe9voux que se les ofrece.","Sean amables y respetuosos con los habitantes de Tr\xe9voux. No duden en pedirles informaci\xf3n o consejo, estar\xe1n encantados de ayudarles.","Aseg\xfarense de que su tel\xe9fono tenga suficiente bater\xeda antes de comenzar su visita. Tambi\xe9n pueden llevar una bater\xeda externa para evitar interrupciones.","Tras su visita, no duden en enviarnos sus comentarios y sugerencias para mejorar la aplicaci\xf3n y los recorridos de visita.","Est\xe1n cruzando ahora la Puerta de Villars, \xa1\xfanico vestigio de las antiguas fortificaciones de Tr\xe9voux! Esta puerta medieval, situada al noreste, es la \xfaltima superviviente de las cuatro puertas que antiguamente permit\xedan entrar en la ciudad fortificada. Las otras tres \u2014la puerta de Lyon al este, la puerta del Saona al sur y la puerta de Saint-Bernard al oeste\u2014 desaparecieron lamentablemente con el paso de los siglos.","Construida en piedra dorada y ladrillo, esta puerta estaba integrada en la muralla que rodeaba por completo la ciudad en la \xe9poca del Principado de Dombes. Debe su nombre a los se\xf1ores de Villars, que dominaron la regi\xf3n desde el siglo XII, antes de unirse con los se\xf1ores de Thoire, dando origen al linaje de los Thoire-Villars, que finalmente vendi\xf3 el feudo a los Borb\xf3n en 1402.","Estas fortificaciones no eran solo un s\xedmbolo: respond\xedan a una necesidad militar real. Los ataques repetidos desde Saboya y Borgo\xf1a justificaban esta protecci\xf3n. Cada puerta estaba vigilada, controlada y cerrada por la noche. Atravesar esta puerta significaba entrar en un principado soberano, \xa1con sus propias leyes y su propia moneda! Hoy en d\xeda, nos recuerda que Tr\xe9voux fue mucho m\xe1s que un simple pueblo: una aut\xe9ntica ciudad-estado en pleno coraz\xf3n de la Europa medieval.","\xa1Las puertas de las ciudades en la Edad Media eran mucho m\xe1s que simples aberturas en las murallas! Constitu\xedan aut\xe9nticos puestos de control donde se ejerc\xedan los derechos se\xf1oriales. Los guardias verificaban la identidad de los viajeros, cobraban impuestos de entrada y controlaban las mercanc\xedas. Cada puerta ten\xeda sus propios horarios: apertura al amanecer, cierre al atardecer. \xa1Llegar de noche significaba dormir fuera! Estas puertas sol\xedan estar flanqueadas por torres y equipadas con rastrillos, puentes levadizos y aspilleras. Marcaban la frontera entre el mundo exterior y el espacio urbano protegido.","\xa1La construcci\xf3n de las murallas supon\xeda una inversi\xf3n colosal para las ciudades medievales! Hab\xeda que movilizar a cientos de trabajadores durante a\xf1os, extraer y transportar miles de toneladas de piedra, y organizar trabajos forzados entre los habitantes. En Tr\xe9voux, la muralla combinaba ladrillo y piedra, seg\xfan una t\xe9cnica muy extendida en la regi\xf3n. \xa1Estas fortificaciones pesaron durante a\xf1os sobre las finanzas municipales! Pero eran vitales: una ciudad sin fortificar estaba a merced del primer se\xf1or de la guerra que pasara por all\xed. Las murallas eran, por tanto, una garant\xeda de prosperidad e independencia.",'\xa1El nombre de las puertas se eleg\xeda con esmero y revelaba la organizaci\xf3n geogr\xe1fica de la \xe9poca! La puerta de Lyon llevaba hacia esa gran ciudad, la puerta del Saona hacia el r\xedo, la puerta de Saint-Bernard hacia ese pueblo vecino. Esta denominaci\xf3n permit\xeda a los viajeros orientarse f\xe1cilmente: "\xa1Tomen la puerta de Lyon si quieren llegar a la gran ruta del sur!". Estos nombres han perdurado en la memoria colectiva y a\xfan hoy dan sus nombres a calles, plazas o barrios. Cuentan la historia de los intercambios comerciales y de las relaciones entre los territorios en la \xe9poca medieval.',"\xbfSalir de la visita?","Tu progreso en este recorrido no se guardar\xe1. Tendr\xe1s que empezar esta etapa de nuevo si vuelves m\xe1s tarde.","Salir de la visita","Continuar la visita","No est\xe1s en el punto de partida","Pareces estar lejos del punto de partida de esta etapa. \xbfQuieres que te indiquemos c\xf3mo llegar?","Ll\xe9vame all\xed","Continuar sin indicaciones","Ir al punto de partida","No se pudo calcular la ruta en este momento.","A pie","En coche","En bici",u.F,"De acuerdo","Recentrar","\xa1Bien hecho, has terminado la visita!","Has recorrido el coraz\xf3n hist\xf3rico de Tr\xe9voux y descubierto su rico patrimonio. \xa1Gracias por participar en esta visita!","{distance} recorridos a pie","\xa1Acabo de terminar la visita de Tr\xe9voux! \ud83c\udff0\ud83d\udeb6","Compartir","Ver mi diario de viaje","Para descubrir","Tus fotos recuerdo","Recompensas","Tus insignias ganadas","Ver mis recompensas","Volver al inicio","N","Ubicaci\xf3n necesaria","Esta funci\xf3n necesita tu ubicaci\xf3n para guiarte y detectar tu llegada. Permite el acceso a la ubicaci\xf3n para continuar.","Se deneg\xf3 el acceso a la ubicaci\xf3n. Abre los ajustes de la app para activarlo y vuelve aqu\xed.","La ubicaci\xf3n (GPS) est\xe1 desactivada en tu tel\xe9fono. Act\xedvala en los ajustes para continuar.","Permitir ubicaci\xf3n","Abrir ajustes de la app","Activar ubicaci\xf3n","Ahora no","Si eliges \xabAhora no\xbb, saldr\xe1s de la visita en curso: la ubicaci\xf3n es imprescindible para continuar el recorrido.","Actualizaci\xf3n necesaria","Hay una nueva versi\xf3n de la aplicaci\xf3n disponible y debe instalarse para continuar.","Actualizar ahora","Informaci\xf3n legal","Aviso legal","Condiciones de uso","Privacidad","La versi\xf3n de referencia de esta pol\xedtica est\xe1 disponible en l\xednea:","Ver en l\xednea","Cerrar","Informaci\xf3n legal","S","O","E","\ud83c\udf33 El Roble del Sabio","\xa1Bienvenido, joven aprendiz de caballero! Cuenta la leyenda que aqu\xed se alzaba un roble centenario, testigo del nacimiento del castillo de Tr\xe9voux. Nadie sabe si esta historia es cierta, pero los ancianos dec\xedan que sus ra\xedces guardaban los secretos de nuestra historia.","\xbfCu\xe1ntas ramas principales tiene este majestuoso roble?","Entre 3 y 4 ramas","Entre 5 y 7 ramas","Entre 8 y 10 ramas","M\xe1s de 10 ramas","Mira bien hacia la copa del \xe1rbol y cuenta solo las ramas m\xe1s gruesas que salen del tronco principal.","\ud83d\udc41\ufe0f La Piedra del Vig\xeda","La leyenda cuenta que una antigua piedra serv\xeda aqu\xed de puesto de vigilancia para los guardias del castillo de Tr\xe9voux, que vigilaban el r\xedo Saona y los caminos hacia la fortaleza. Como muchos caballeros de la \xe9poca, usaban sus propios c\xf3digos y s\xedmbolos para reconocerse.","\xbfQu\xe9 grababan principalmente los caballeros en sus escudos para distinguirse en combate?","Espadas cruzadas","Sus blasones familiares","Torres de castillo","Flores de lis reales","Cada familia noble ten\xeda sus propios colores y s\xedmbolos hereditarios para ser reconocida.","\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f El \xc1rbol de los Blasones","Se dice que un viejo \xe1rbol de este bosque llevaba anta\xf1o escudos tallados en su corteza, en memoria de los se\xf1ores de Tr\xe9voux. Como todos los nobles, ten\xedan su propio blas\xf3n, que adornaba escudos, estandartes y muros del castillo.","\xbfCu\xe1les eran los colores tradicionales m\xe1s nobles utilizados en los blasones medievales?","Rojo y oro (oro amarillo)","Azul y plata (blanco)","Verde y violeta","Solo blanco y negro","Los metales preciosos (oro y plata) se consideraban los colores m\xe1s nobles en her\xe1ldica.","\ud83c\udf3f El Bosquecillo de los Herboristas","Seg\xfan la leyenda, los monjes del castillo vinieron aqu\xed a cultivar un jard\xedn de plantas medicinales, tan preciadas en la Edad Media. Su saber en bot\xe1nica habr\xeda sido inmenso, curando a los habitantes de Tr\xe9voux con remedios naturales.","\xbfQu\xe9 planta era especialmente famosa en la Edad Media para curar dolores de cabeza y mejorar la memoria?","La menta fresca","El tomillo silvestre","La salvia oficinal","Todas estas plantas","Los monjes conoc\xedan bien las virtudes de muchas plantas arom\xe1ticas de nuestras regiones.","\ud83d\udc8e El Claro del Tesoro","\xa1Felicidades, valiente caballero! Acabas de atravesar el claro secreto de los guardianes del bosque de Tr\xe9voux, al menos seg\xfan cuenta la leyenda. Aqu\xed termina tu recorrido, pero recuerda que la verdadera aventura solo comienza cuando te lanzas a descubrir nuestro patrimonio.","Seg\xfan la sabidur\xeda de los antiguos caballeros, \xbfcu\xe1l es el mayor tesoro que un h\xe9roe puede descubrir?","Un cofre lleno de oro","Una espada m\xe1gica","El conocimiento y la sabidur\xeda","Un pergamino de secretos","Los verdaderos h\xe9roes saben que la riqueza m\xe1s preciosa no se mide en monedas de oro.","Insignia del Sabio","Insignia del Vig\xeda","Insignia de los Blasones","Insignia del Herborista","Insignia del Tesoro","El Mapa del Bosque","Ver mi tesoro","El Roble de los Secretos","Juego de memoria","Bajo sus viejas ra\xedces, el Roble esconde parejas de secretos. \xa1Encu\xe9ntralas todas para ganarte su confianza!","La Piedra del Vig\xeda","Acertijos del bosque","El Vig\xeda cuida el bosque desde siempre. Responde sus acertijos para demostrar tu sabidur\xeda.","Soplo sin que nadie me vea jam\xe1s, hago bailar las hojas y viajar las semillas. \xbfQu\xe9 soy?","La lluvia","El viento","El sol","El r\xedo","Llevo mi casa a cuestas y dejo un camino brillante detr\xe1s de m\xed. \xbfQu\xe9 soy?","El erizo","La babosa","El caracol","El lagarto","Cuanto m\xe1s envejezco, m\xe1s crezco. Mis brazos tocan el cielo y mis pies beben la tierra. \xbfQu\xe9 soy?","El \xe1rbol","El r\xedo","La monta\xf1a","La nube","El \xc1rbol de los Blasones","Juego de ritmo","Observa bien el paso de los guardianes del bosque y luego repite su ronda en el orden correcto.","La Arboleda de los Herbolarios","Juego de clasificaci\xf3n","\xa1Un duende travieso mezcl\xf3 su tesoro con sus bromas! Ayuda al Herbolario a distinguir lo real de lo falso.","Tesoro real","Broma de duende","Una fresa silvestre","Un ar\xe1ndano","Una casta\xf1a","Una m\xe1scara de bromista","Una baraja trucada","Una bola de cristal","El Claro del Tesoro","Prueba final","\xa1El cofre se ha roto en pedazos! Toca dos piezas para intercambiarlas y reconstruye la imagen del tesoro.","\xbfAbandonar la b\xfasqueda?","Tu progreso ya est\xe1 guardado, pero este minijuego volver\xe1 a empezar si regresas.","Salir","Seguir jugando","Continuar","\xa1Insignia obtenida!","No del todo... \xa1int\xe9ntalo de nuevo!","{count} movimientos","Observa bien...","\xa1Tu turno!","La B\xfasqueda del Bosque","\xa1Bienvenido, joven aventurero! Soy el guardi\xe1n de este bosque encantado. Explora mis 5 claros, resuelve sus pruebas y descubre el tesoro escondido al final del camino.","Comenzar la aventura","\xa1Toca el primer claro para empezar!","\xa1Sigue hacia el pr\xf3ximo claro!","\xa1Bien hecho, aventurero! Has explorado todos los claros, \xa1ve a buscar tu tesoro!","Vas por la mitad, \xa1sigue as\xed!","\xa1Bien hecho! \xa1Siguiente ronda!","\xa1Ya casi! \xa1\xdaltima ronda!","Omitir esta actividad","\xa1Bienvenido al bosque de Tr\xe9voux! Aqu\xed se cuentan viejas leyendas, transmitidas de generaci\xf3n en generaci\xf3n. Nadie sabe qu\xe9 es verdad, pero merecen ser contadas. Desc\xfabrelas, cap\xedtulo a cap\xedtulo.","Comenzar la misi\xf3n","Tiempo restante: "," etapas","\xbfListo para descubrir la siguiente parte de la leyenda?","Descubrir este cap\xedtulo","Reiniciar la misi\xf3n","\xbfNecesitas una pista?","\xa1Bien hecho! \xa1Respuesta correcta!","\xa1Int\xe9ntalo de nuevo! Usa la pista si es necesario.","\xa1Un nuevo cap\xedtulo te espera!","Contenido en franc\xe9s","La b\xfasqueda en el bosque solo est\xe1 disponible en franc\xe9s por ahora (texto y audio). Puedes acceder igualmente, o saltarte esta etapa.","Acceder de todos modos","Saltar","El Bosque Encantado","\xbfSalir de la visita?","\xbfEst\xe1s seguro de que quieres salir de la visita?","Cancelar","Salir","Saltar la b\xfasqueda","\xbfSaltar la b\xfasqueda del bosque?","Siempre podr\xe1s volver en otro momento. \xbfSaltar de todos modos?","S\xed, saltar","No, continuar la b\xfasqueda","\xa1Felicidades, Caballero!","\xa1Has completado brillantemente la Misi\xf3n de los Guardianes del Bosque de Tr\xe9voux! Tu valent\xeda y sabidur\xeda te han llevado a la victoria.","\xa1Se acab\xf3 el tiempo!","El tiempo asignado para tu misi\xf3n se ha agotado, \xa1pero no te desanimes! Cada aventura es una oportunidad para aprender. \xa1Puedes volver a empezar para mejorar tu puntuaci\xf3n!"," etapas completadas de "," insignias obtenidas","No se recogi\xf3 ninguna insignia esta vez.\n\xa1Vuelve a intentarlo para tener otra oportunidad!","Reiniciar la misi\xf3n","Continuar la visita","Compartir mi diploma","\xa1Super\xe9 el desaf\xedo de la B\xfasqueda de los Guardianes del Bosque de Tr\xe9voux! \ud83c\udfc6\ud83c\udf33","\xa1Tu opini\xf3n nos importa!","Acabas de terminar tu visita. Una rese\xf1a en la tienda nos ayuda much\xedsimo a mejorar la aplicaci\xf3n y a darla a conocer.","Dar mi opini\xf3n","M\xe1s tarde","\xa1Pr\xf3ximamente!",u.F,"De acuerdo","Pr\xf3ximamente","Nuestros lugares","Nuestros lugares","Recorridos","Lista","Mapa","Ver ficha completa","\xa1Destino alcanzado!","Has llegado a {place}. \xbfListo para descubrir este lugar?","Descubrir el lugar","Ll\xe9vame all\xed","Navegando\u2026","Danos tu opini\xf3n","Lo recomiendo","No es para m\xed","\xbfUn comentario? (opcional)","Enviar","\xa1Gracias por tu opini\xf3n!","Tu comentario ser\xe1 visible tras una breve revisi\xf3n.","Cerrar","No se pudo enviar tu opini\xf3n en este momento.","Este comentario no se puede enviar tal cual.","Informar de un problema","Informar de un problema","\xbfCu\xe1l es el problema?","C\xf3digo QR ilegible o roto","El GPS no se activa","Problema con la audiogu\xeda","Error en un texto o una foto","Otro","Describe el problema (opcional)","Enviar el informe","Informe enviado","Gracias, lo revisaremos r\xe1pidamente.","Error al enviar. Comprueba tu conexi\xf3n e int\xe9ntalo de nuevo.","Reintentar","Cerrar","Opiniones","El {percent}% de los visitantes lo recomienda","\xa1S\xe9 el primero en dar tu opini\xf3n!","\xa1Ya hay opiniones sobre este lugar!","Danos tu opini\xf3n","Ya has dado tu opini\xf3n sobre este lugar","Descubre el emblem\xe1tico castillo de Tr\xe9voux, testigo de la historia de la Dombes y antigua sede del parlamento.","Visita esta hermosa iglesia g\xf3tica y descubre su rico patrimonio art\xedstico y espiritual.","Admira esta torre hist\xf3rica que domina la ciudad, orgullosa en el coraz\xf3n de la villa.","Disfruta de un panorama excepcional sobre el valle del Saona y los montes del Beaujolais.","Cruza esta puerta medieval, vestigio de las antiguas fortificaciones de la ciudad.","Sum\xe9rgete en la historia del patrimonio local con este magn\xedfico lavadero restaurado del siglo XIX.","Disfruta de una parada en este magn\xedfico parlamento de las Dombes y sus magn\xedficos frescos.","Descubre esta emblem\xe1tica calle de Tr\xe9voux y sus talleres art\xedsticos.","Audiogu\xeda","Audiogu\xeda disponible","Audiogu\xeda no disponible en tu idioma","\xbfHas llegado?","Comprobando tu ubicaci\xf3n","Parece que todav\xeda est\xe1s a {distance} del lugar. Ac\xe9rcate, o confirma si ya has llegado.","No podemos comprobar tu ubicaci\xf3n en este momento (sin se\xf1al GPS). Puedes volver a intentarlo, o continuar si ya has llegado.","Continuar de todos modos","Reintentar","\xbfQuieres vivir toda la visita?","Descarga la aplicaci\xf3n de Tr\xe9voux para seguir el recorrido completo, desbloquear los retos y mucho m\xe1s.","Descargar para Android","Descargar para iPhone","Acerca de","Galer\xeda de fotos","Escanear un c\xf3digo QR","Escanear","Escanea el c\xf3digo QR de un lugar para acceder directamente","C\xf3digo QR no reconocido","Escaneo cancelado","Pr\xf3xima parada","Duraci\xf3n de la etapa: ","Tiempo total restante: "," min","Continuar","El Bosque Encantado","Fin del recorrido","\xbfReanudar tu visita?","Tienes un recorrido en curso. \xbfQuieres continuar donde lo dejaste o empezar de nuevo?","Reanudar","Empezar de nuevo","\xa1Est\xe1s en Tr\xe9voux!","Aprovecha para descubrir la ciudad con nuestro recorrido guiado.","Descubrir ahora","M\xe1s tarde","Diario de viaje","Mi diario de viaje","Una foto recuerdo por cada lugar visitado \u2014 toca el icono de la c\xe1mara para a\xf1adir una.","Insignias del bosque","Hacer una foto","Elegir de la galer\xeda","\xbfEliminar esta foto?","Esta foto de recuerdo se eliminar\xe1 definitivamente del diario de viaje.","Eliminar","Cancelar","Compartir mi certificado","Mi diario de viaje por Tr\xe9voux","Un recuerdo de tu paso por la ciudad","Compartir mi diario","Descargar","Tu recuerdo de Tr\xe9voux","Diario de viaje","Tr\xe9voux","Vivido con Flan\xe9a, la app que te hace descubrir Tr\xe9voux de otra manera.","\xa1Imagen guardada en la galer\xeda!","No se pudo guardar la imagen.","Generando imagen...","\xa1Inmortaliza este momento!","Haz una foto recuerdo de este lugar: se queda en la aplicaci\xf3n, a\xf1adida a tu diario de viaje personal. Puedes consultarla en cualquier momento, y descargar el diario completo al final del recorrido.","Hacer una foto","M\xe1s tarde","Favorito","\xbfCu\xe1ntas pilas ves en el lavadero?","Mira bien dentro, est\xe1n una al lado de la otra.","\xa1Bien visto!","\xbfCu\xe1ntos pisos tiene la torre del reloj?","Levanta la vista y cuenta los niveles, de abajo hacia arriba.","\xa1Exacto, qu\xe9 buen observador!","Verdadero o falso: un roble puede vivir m\xe1s de 100 a\xf1os.","Piensa en el tama\xf1o y la edad de los \xe1rboles m\xe1s grandes que conoces.","\xa1Muy bien, peque\xf1o naturalista!","\xbfQu\xe9 forma tiene la abertura de la puerta?","Redonda, en arco","Cuadrada","Triangular","Mira la parte de arriba de la abertura: \xbfes recta o curva?","\xa1Buena observaci\xf3n!","\xbfCu\xe1ntas torres ves en el castillo?","Mira a tu alrededor sin mover los pies.","\xa1Genial, las encontraste todas!","\xbfQu\xe9 ves en el horizonte desde este mirador?","Mira muy lejos, m\xe1s all\xe1 de los tejados.","\xa1Precioso, tienes muy buen ojo!","\xbfQu\xe9 s\xedmbolo ves en la fachada de la iglesia?","Una cruz","Una estrella","Un escudo","Mira bien arriba, en el centro de la fachada.","\xa1Bien visto, campe\xf3n!","\xa1Crea tu h\xe9roe!","\xbfC\xf3mo te llamas?","Tu nombre","Elige tu avatar","Caballero","Princesa","Explorador","Mago","\xa1Hola {name}!","piezas de puzle","Continuar la aventura","\xa1Bien hecho, has terminado todas las etapas!","Bloqueado","En curso","Terminado","\xbfNecesitas una pista?","Saltar","\xbfSaltar este reto?","Siempre puedes volver a intentarlo otro d\xeda. \xbfSaltar de todos modos?","S\xed, saltar","No, lo intento de nuevo","\xa1Casi! Int\xe9ntalo de nuevo \ud83d\udcaa","Verdadero","Falso","Confirmar","\xa1Nueva pieza de puzle!","\xa1Acepta el reto!","\xa1Ya casi llegas, sigue as\xed!","\xa1Enhorabuena, {name}!","\xa1Has completado el Recorrido l\xfadico de Tr\xe9voux con \xe9xito!","Diploma de aventurero","certifica que {name} explor\xf3 los secretos de Tr\xe9voux y super\xf3 todos los retos del Recorrido l\xfadico.","\xa1He terminado el Recorrido l\xfadico de Tr\xe9voux con {name}! \ud83c\udfc6\ud83e\udde9","Compartir","\xa1Rasca la pantalla con el dedo para revelar tu puzle!","Revelar todo","Volver al inicio","Girar la ruleta de premios","Ruleta de premios pr\xf3ximamente","Recorrido l\xfadico","Duraci\xf3n","Edad recomendada","Nivel f\xedsico","\xbfPara qui\xe9n?","Cancelar","Aqu\xed tienes el recorrido","Un diario de viaje para ti","Durante la visita, la aplicaci\xf3n te propondr\xe1 tomar una foto en cada lugar. Se queda en la aplicaci\xf3n, a\xf1adida a tu diario de viaje personal: disponible en cualquier momento, y descargable al final del recorrido.","Recorrido no accesible con cochecitos.","Entre 1h30 y 2h aproximadamente","A partir de 12 a\xf1os recomendado",u.B,"Para todos los p\xfablicos","Descubre los tesoros escondidos de Tr\xe9voux en un paseo guiado: castillo, torre del reloj, lavadero y mucho m\xe1s, a tu ritmo.","Entre 1h30 y 2h aproximadamente","A partir de 6 a\xf1os",u.B,"En familia, con los ni\xf1os","\xa1Vive el recorrido cultural en modo juego! Tu h\xe9roe supera un reto en cada lugar, recoge piezas de puzle y recibe un diploma al final de la aventura."],t.l)
